hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1201","Among what Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab narrated from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father: Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih told us, saying: al-Layth ibn Sa'd told us, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while there were women of Quraysh with him, their voices raised above his voice. When Umar sought permission, they hastened to the veil. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him permission, and Umar entered while the Messenger of Allah was laughing. Umar said: May Allah keep your teeth smiling — by my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah — what made you laugh? He said: ""I was amazed at these women who were with me; when they heard your voice they hastened to the veil."" So Umar said: You were more deserving that they should stand in awe of you, O Messenger of Allah. Then Umar said: O enemies of your own selves! Do you stand in awe of me and not stand in awe of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: Yes — you are harsher and sterner than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O son of al-Khattab! By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Satan never meets you walking upon a path but he takes a path other than yours."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1202","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun told us, saying: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah told us, from Yahya ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two leather socks. And we do not know anyone to have narrated from Yahya ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad, except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from him except al-Hajjaj."
"1203","Among what Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated from his father, from his grandfather: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abu Ahmad told us, saying: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq told us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the supplication of Dhu al-Nun. He said: And a Bedouin came and distracted him, so he stood up and I followed him, and he turned to me and said: ""Abu Ishaq?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""What is it?"" I said: You mentioned the supplication of Dhu al-Nun, then a Bedouin came and distracted you. He said: ""Yes. The supplication of Dhu al-Nun when he called out in the belly of the whale: There is no god but You; glory be to You; indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers — for no Muslim ever supplicates with it for anything but he is answered."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Muhammad ibn Sa'd except from the narration of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather. And it is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the narration of Sa'd, from him. And it has been narrated from Sa'd through two channels."
"1204","What Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa narrated from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father Sa'd: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, known as Ibn Abi Ali al-Kirmani, narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Awn told us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah told us, from al-Shaybani, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Part of happiness is: a righteous wife, a spacious dwelling, and a comfortable mount."" This hadith is only known from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather — and with this chain it is not established. I have not seen anyone narrate this hadith relying upon it, and Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Kirmani was not followed in it. Nor did Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa narrate, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, any hadith — rather we left it for this defect."
"1205","Among what Umar ibn Sa'd narrated from his father Sa'd — al-Muttalib from Umar from his father: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir told us, saying: Kathir ibn Zayd told us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father, that a comer came to him and said: This one has been besieged by your people — meaning Uthman — while Uthman is besieged in his house. He said: So what do you command me — that I be one who unsheathes the sword? By Allah, I shall not do so until I am given a sword with which, when I strike a believer, it turns away from him, and when I strike a disbeliever with it, I kill him. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Indeed, Allah loves the rich, God-fearing, obscure one."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Sa'd, from him. And we do not know for it, from Sa'd, any route better than this route. And we do not know that al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab narrated, from Umar, from his father, except this hadith."
"1206","Among what al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth narrated from Umar ibn Sa'd from his father: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, from Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"1207","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I marvel at Allah's decree for the believer: if good befalls him, he praises Allah and gives thanks; and if calamity befalls him, he praises Allah and is patient. So the believer is rewarded in everything — even in the morsel he raises to his wife's mouth."" And we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd with a sound chain except through this channel. And it has been narrated from Suhayb and from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith we have already mentioned from the hadith of al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Mus'ab, from his father — while the correct one is what Shu'bah and al-Thawri narrated from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar, from Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"1208","Among what Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrated from Umar ibn Sa'd from his father: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa told us, saying: Badr ibn Uthman told us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You shall be granted martyrdom through killing, plague, drowning, abdominal illness, and the death of a woman in childbed: her death in her postpartum."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1209","And Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa told us, saying: Badr ibn Uthman told us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever claims (descent) from other than his father"" — I think he said: ""and attaches himself to other than his masters — Paradise is forbidden to him."""
"1210","What an unnamed man narrated from Umar ibn Sa'd from his father: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan told us, saying: Abu Hayyan al-Taymi told us, saying: A man — I have forgotten his name — told me, from Umar ibn Sa'd, that he had a need from his father, so he set out and strung words together, then came to Sa'd and spoke to him with speech he had never heard from him before. When he finished, Sa'd said to him: Have you finished stating your need? He said: Yes. He said: ""You were never farther from your need than you are now, nor was I ever more averse to you than I am now. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall be a people who eat with their tongues as cattle eat with their tongues."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel."
"1211","Among what Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated from his father Sa'd — Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah from Ibrahim from his father: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Jarir told us, saying: My father told me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd told me, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out from Medina to Tabuk, he left Ali ibn Abi Talib behind — may Allah be pleased with him. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, will you leave me behind after you, when I have never stayed behind from you in any expedition? He said: ""O Ali, return."" So he said: O Messenger of Allah, the hypocrites are saying you left me behind out of dislike. So he said: ""O Ali, are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me? So return and remain behind in my place over my family and yours."" And we do not know that Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid narrated, from Ibrahim, from his father, except this hadith."
"1212","Among what Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd from his father: I heard Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd say: Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asadi told us, saying: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, told us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from his father — thus Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated it from Sufyan, from Amr, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from his father. While others besides Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrate it only from Sufyan, from Amr, from Muhammad ibn Ali, as mursal, saying: There were a people with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Ali came. When Ali entered, they went out. When they went out, they blamed one another, and some said to others: By Allah, it was not we who made us go out — so let us return. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Allah, it was not I who brought him in and brought you out; rather, Allah brought him in and brought you out."""
"1213","Among what Yahya ibn Sa'd narrated from his father Sa'd — Ikrimah ibn Khalid from Yahya ibn Sa'd from his father: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Mu'adh ibn Hisham told us, saying: My father told me, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Yahya ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When plague is in a land, do not descend upon it; and when it breaks out in a land while you are in it, do not leave it."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'd, from his father, except Ikrimah ibn Khalid. And it was narrated from Ikrimah by Qatadah and others — so we sufficed with the hadith of Qatadah."
"1214","Among what Kharijah ibn Sa'd narrated from his father — al-Hasan ibn Zayd from Kharijah ibn Sa'd from his father: Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways told us, saying: My father told me, from al-Hasan ibn Zayd, from Kharijah ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: ""It is not lawful for anyone in a state of major impurity to be in this mosque except me and you."" These words, we do not know them to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain. And Kharijah ibn Sa'd has narrated another hadith with this chain. And we do not know anyone to have narrated from Kharijah ibn Sa'd except this al-Hasan ibn Zayd."
"1215","Among what A'ishah bint Sa'd narrated from her father — Abu al-Zinad from A'ishah from her father: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Jarir told us, saying: My father told us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Abu al-Zinad, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he took the road of al-Far', would enter ihram when his mount stood upright with him; and when he took another road, he would enter ihram when he ascended the height of al-Bayda'. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel. And we do not know that Abu al-Zinad narrated, from A'ishah, from her father, except this hadith. And we do not know anyone to have narrated this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Sa'd."
"1216","Among what Abdullah ibn Ubaydah narrated from A'ishah from her father: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Yunus told us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from his brother Abdullah ibn Ubaydah, from A'ishah, daughter of Sa'd, from her father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and the nights and days shall not pass until my nation splits into the like thereof."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel. And we do not know that Abdullah ibn Ubaydah narrated, from A'ishah, from her father, except this hadith."
"1217","Among what al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated from A'ishah from her father: Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad told us, from Layth, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from A'ishah, from her father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali in the expedition of Tabuk: ""Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"" And we do not know anyone to have narrated this hadith from Layth except al-Muttalib, with this chain. Nor did al-Hakam narrate, from A'ishah, from her father, except this hadith. And the correct one is what Shu'bah narrated from al-Hakam, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"1218","Among what Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal narrated from A'ishah from her father: Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, saying: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj told us, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith told me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, that he entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a woman, and before her were date-stones or pebbles with which she was glorifying Allah. So he said: ""Shall I not tell you of what is easier for you than this, or better?"" She said: Yes. He said: ""Say: Glory be to Allah to the number of what He created in the heaven, and glory be to Allah to the number of what He created on the earth, and glory be to Allah to the number of what is between that, and glory be to Allah as He deserves; and Allah is Most Great likewise, and there is no god but Allah likewise, and all praise is due to Allah likewise, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah likewise."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1219","Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tamimi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abdullah told us, saying: al-Layth told us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand; and begin with those you support."""
"1220","Among what Muhajir ibn Mismar narrated from A'ishah from her father: Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Uthmah told us, saying: Musa ibn Ya'qub told us, saying: Muhajir ibn Mismar told us, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took Ali by the hand and said: ""Am I not more entitled to the believers than their own selves? Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the hadith of A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, except through this channel. And we do not know that al-Muhajir ibn Mismar narrated, from A'ishah, from her father, except this hadith."
"1221","Among what al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated from A'ishah from her father: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan told us, from al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, who said: I fell ill in Mecca, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me visiting me. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have left none but a daughter — shall I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth? He said: ""No."" He said: Shall I bequeath half? He said: ""No."" He said: Shall I bequeath a third and leave her two-thirds? He said: ""A third — and a third is much"" — three times. He said: And he placed his hand on my forehead and my face and my chest, and wiped my face and my chest and my belly, and said: ""Heal Sa'd, and complete his emigration for him."" And I have continued, until this very hour, to imagine I feel the coolness of his hand upon my liver. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated with this wording, from Sa'd, except through this channel."
"1222","Among what Ubaydah bint Nabil narrated from A'ishah bint Sa'd from her father: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya, the companion of al-Sabiri, narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi told us, saying: Ubaydah bint Nabil told me, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, who said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking while standing."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel. And this Ubaydah, daughter of Nabil — Ma'n ibn Isa, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi, and Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani have narrated from her."
"1223","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Muhammad told us, saying: Ubaydah bint Nabil told me, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What is between my house and my pulpit — or my grave and my pulpit — is a garden of the gardens of Paradise."" This hadith has been narrated by Ubaydah, and it was also narrated by Junah, the freedman of Layla, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father."
"1224","Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Muhammad told us, from Ubaydah bint Nabil, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1225","And Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi told us, saying: Ubaydah bint Nabil told us, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in Mecca on the day he conquered it eight rak'ahs, prolonging the recitation therein, and the bowing."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1226","Abu Kurayb and Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Yazid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman told us, saying: Umm Abdullah — meaning Ubaydah bint Nabil — told us, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, who said: ""We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he found two dates, so he took one date and gave me the other."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel."
"1227","And I heard Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrating from Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi, saying: Ma'n ibn Isa told us, saying: Ubaydah bint Nabil told me, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had food before him, and said: ""O Allah, bring to this food a servant whom You love and who loves You."" He said: So he appeared — meaning himself. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated with this wording except from Sa'd, with this chain. While in other than the hadith of Ubaydah, from A'ishah, from her father: Abdullah ibn Salam appeared."
"1228","Among what Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn al-Miswar ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated from A'ishah from her father: al-Abbas ibn Abi Talib al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Atiyyah told us, saying: Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn al-Miswar ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf told us, saying: A'ishah bint Sa'd told me, from her father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever recites {Say: He is Allah, One}, it is as if he recited a third of the Qur'an."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1229","Among what Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan narrated from A'ishah, from her father: Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad told us, saying: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn al-Hasan told us, saying: My uncle Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan told me, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There shall come a people who eat with their tongues as cattle eat with their tongues."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father, except Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan."
"1230","Among what Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated from A'ishah bint Sa'd from her father: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Bukayr told us, saying: Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman told us, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father Sa'd, who said: When the people scattered from around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud, I said: I shall hold firm — either I am martyred or I survive — until I meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While I was thus, there was a man with his face covered, and I did not know who he was. The idolaters came toward him, and I said: They have mounted him? Then he filled his hand with pebbles and threw them at their faces, and they turned back on their heels retreating, until they passed by and came level with the mountain. He did that repeatedly, while I did not know who he was. Between me and him was al-Miqdad. While I was about to ask al-Miqdad about him, al-Miqdad said: O Sa'd, this is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling you. So I said: And where is he? So al-Miqdad pointed to him for me, and I stood up — as if nothing of harm had befallen me. So he said: ""Where have you been since today, O Sa'd?"" And he seated me before him, and I sat shooting, saying: O Allah, an arrow with which I strike Your enemy — while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying: ""O Allah, answer Sa'd; O Allah, make his aim true. Go on, Sa'd — may my father and mother be ransom for you."" There was no arrow I shot but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, make his aim true and answer his supplication. Go on, Sa'd."" Until when I had emptied my quiver, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) scattered his quiver for me and handed me an arrow without feathers on it, and it was more piercing than others. Al-Zuhri said: The arrows Sa'd shot that day were a thousand arrows. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd with this wording except through this channel with this chain."
"1231","Among what Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrated from Sa'd — Isma'il from Qays from Sa'd: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id told us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid told us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sa'd, who said: ""I am the first of the Arabs to shoot an arrow in the cause of Allah. And you have seen us raiding with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with no food to eat except the leaves of the hubalah and this samur, until one of us would pass stool like sheep pass stool, with no mixture in it. Then Banu Asad began to reproach me concerning the religion — then I would indeed be ruined and my deed lost."" This hadith has been narrated from Isma'il, from Qays, from Sa'd, by Shu'bah as well and others. And we do not know anyone to have narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Sa'd. And Utbah ibn Ghazwan narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something close to it."
"1232","Yahya ibn al-Fadl al-Khuraqi narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Sa'd, with the like thereof."
"1233","And Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah told us, saying: Isma'il told us, from Qays, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""There shall ever remain a group of my nation upon the truth, triumphant, until the Day of Resurrection."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Isma'il, from Qays, from Sa'd, except Abu Mu'awiyah. And others besides Abu Mu'awiyah narrated it from Isma'il, from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah."
"1234","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah told us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Sa'd, that he prayed and stood up in the two rak'ahs, so the people glorified Allah (to alert him), and he proceeded in his prayer and did not sit. Then he said when he finished: ""Do you think I would sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."" This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Isma'il, from Qays, from Sa'd, as mawquf. And al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl narrated it from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah."
"1235","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Raja' ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Awn told us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Sa'd, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard me while I was supplicating, and said: ""O Allah, answer him when he calls upon You."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Isma'il, from Qays, from Sa'd, except Ja'far ibn Awn."
"1236","And Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, saying: al-Nadr ibn Isma'il told us, saying: Isma'il told us, from Qays, who said: Sa'd said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never joined his two parents (in the formula 'may my father and mother be ransom for you') for anyone before me. And I saw him while he was saying: O Sa'd, shoot — may my father and mother be ransom for you."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Qays except Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, nor from Isma'il except al-Nadr ibn Isma'il al-Bajali."
"1237","Among what al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl narrated from Qays from Sa'd: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Uthman told us, saying: Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari told us, from Jabir, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr with one rak'ah. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd as marfu' except through this channel. And this al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl is a well-known man of Kufa; a group narrated from him."
"1238","Among what Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated from Sa'd — Asim ibn Sulayman al-Ahwal from Abu Uthman from Sa'd: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah told us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Sa'd and Abu Bakrah — each of them saying: I heard it myself from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Whoever claims (descent) from other than his father while knowing that he is other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Abu Uthman, from Sa'd and Abu Bakrah, except Asim al-Ahwal."
"1239","Among what Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated from Abu Uthman from Sa'd: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab told us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Uthman, from Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people of the West shall ever remain triumphant upon the truth until the Day of Resurrection."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except with this chain."
"1240","And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Rashid told us, saying: Dawud ibn Abi Hind told us. And Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated it to us, saying: Maslamah, meaning Ibn Alqamah, told us, from Dawud, from Abu Uthman, from Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There shall be a trial in which the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel with this chain."
"1241","Among what Umar ibn al-Hakam narrated from Sa'd — Musa ibn Ubaydah from Umar ibn al-Hakam from Sa'd: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah Abu Abd al-Aziz al-Rabadhi, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among the mosques, except al-Masjid al-Haram."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Sa'd, except Musa ibn Ubaydah. And our remark about Musa ibn Ubaydah has already preceded in another place."
"1242","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Jarir told us, saying: My father told us, saying: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If what a fingernail carries of Paradise were to appear to the people of this world, what is between the horizons of the heavens would be adorned for them. And if a man of Paradise were to show his hand, the light of his bracelet would efface the light of the sun, just as the sun effaces the stars."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Umar ibn al-Hakam except Yazid ibn Abi Habib."
"1243","Among what Bakr ibn Qirwash narrated from Sa'd — Abu al-Tufayl from Bakr from Sa'd: Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah told us, from al-Ala' ibn Abi al-Abbas, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Bakr ibn Qirwash, from Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The devil of al-Radhah is a herder of camels, or the son of a herder of camels — a man of Bajilah called al-Ashhab, or Ibn al-Ashhab, shall drag him out — a sign among an unjust people."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Sa'd. And we do not know for it, from Sa'd, any chain except this chain."
"1244","Among what Shurayh ibn Hani' narrated from Sa'd: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id told us, from Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Sa'd, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the idolaters said: Look — he brings these near to the exclusion of us. And I was with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, a man of Hudhayl, and two men whose names I have forgotten. So it entered the heart of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he spoke to himself of it — so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: {And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His Face} — up to: {And thus We tried some of them with others}. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1245","Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Tuhawi narrated to us, saying: al-Waddah ibn Yahya told us, saying: Qays told us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Sa'd, who said: ""The people used to ask about something of the affair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or they would ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while it was lawful — and they kept asking about it until it was forbidden to them."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the hadith of al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, except from the hadith of Qays, from him."
"1246","Among what the shaykhs narrated from Sa'd: Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl told us, saying: Yunus ibn Amr — he is Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq — told us, from Abdullah ibn Jabir, from the nephew of Sa'd ibn Malik, from Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The Muslims shall prevail over Rome, and the Muslims shall prevail over Persia, and the Muslims shall prevail over the Arabian Peninsula."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except with this chain. And this Abdullah ibn Jabir — we do not know anyone to have narrated from him except Yunus ibn Amr."
"1247","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi told us, saying: Hafs ibn al-Nadr told us, saying: Amir ibn Kharijah ibn Sa'd told us, from his grandfather Sa'd, that a people complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of lack of rain, so he commanded them to kneel upon their knees. He said: ""Say: O Lord, O Lord"" — so they did, and they were given rain until they wished it to be withheld from them. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated except from Sa'd. And we do not know for it, from Sa'd, any route except this route. And I do not think Amir ibn Kharijah heard anything from his grandfather."
"1248","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Jarir told us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Nawfal, who said: I heard al-Dahhak ibn Qays, in the year Mu'awiyah performed hajj, asking Sa'd about the hajj tamattu', and he said: Umar used to forbid it. So Sa'd said: Rather, one better than Umar did it — the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it. This hadith has been narrated from Sa'd, and this chain is among the best chains narrated from Sa'd."
"1249","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, saying: Malik told us, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Zayd Abu Ayyash, who said: I asked Sa'd about white wheat for barley, and he disliked it. And he narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about fresh dates for dry dates, and said: ""Does it diminish?"" They said: Yes. So he forbade it. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1250","And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah told us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Nahik, from Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an melodiously."" This hadith from Sa'd — we do not know for it any chain better than this chain."
"1251","And Isma'il ibn Hafs narrated to us, saying: al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr told us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Recite the Qur'an and weep; and if you do not weep, then force yourselves to weep."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain. And this Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr is weak in hadith."
"1252","And Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Dawud told us, saying: al-A'mash told us, from Abu Salih, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man gesturing with two fingers, and said: ""One, one."" Thus Abu Mu'awiyah and Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated it. And Hafs narrated it from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah."
"1253","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Simak, who said: I heard a man whose uncle was Sa'd — once saying from Sa'd — who said: I mentioned Banu Najiyah before the Prophet (peace be upon him). Either the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The very eye wept — Samah ibn Lu'ayy"" — then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The bond has attached itself to Samah, the attachment"" — or the man said it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). These words, we do not know them to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel."
"1254","Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, saying: Mis'ar told us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Sa'd, who said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud, with a man on his right and a man on his left, wearing white garments — I had never seen them before nor after."" None narrated this from the Prophet (peace be upon him) except Sa'd. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain. And we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Mis'ar except Abu Bakr al-Hanafi and Muhammad ibn Ubayd."
"1255","And Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah told us, saying: al-Shaybani told us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, meaning al-Thaqafi, from Sa'd, who said: On the day of Uhud I killed Sa'id ibn al-As, and I took his sword — and it was a sword of value. He said: So I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while my brother Umayr had been killed before that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Go and cast it"" — meaning into the spoils. He said: So I returned, with in me what none but Allah knows of the killing of my brother and the taking of my spoils. He said: I had gone only a short distance when Surat al-Anfal came down — so the Prophet (peace be upon him) called me and said: ""Go and take your sword."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel."
"1256","Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Bashir told us, saying: Mujalid told us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Sa'd, who said: ""The first commander appointed in Islam was Abdullah ibn Jahsh — the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed him over us."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel."
"1257","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Muhabbab Abu Hammam told us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri told us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from Sa'd, that the women said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a burden upon our sons and fathers and husbands — so what is lawful for us from their wealth? He said: ""Fresh produce — you may eat it and give it as a gift."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from the Prophet (peace be upon him) except Sa'd, with this chain."
"1258","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi al-Wazir told us, saying: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, told us, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Kathir, from Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""If a man were killed in the cause of Allah, then brought back to life, then killed again — he would not enter Paradise until his debt is settled."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel. And some of the companions of Abd al-Aziz have narrated it from Abd al-Aziz, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Kathir, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Jahsh, from the Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"1259","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Safwan ibn Isa told us, saying: Umar ibn Nubayh told us, from Dinar al-Qarraz, from Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever intends harm to the people of Medina, Allah shall melt him as salt melts in water."" This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Dinar al-Qarraz, from Sa'd."
"1260","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan told us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, from Sa'd, that he heard a man saying: ""Labbayk, O Possessor of the Ascensions"" — so he said: ""He is indeed the Possessor of the Ascensions, but we did not use to say this with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" Thus Yahya narrated it."
"1261","And al-Darawardi narrated it from Ibn Ajlan, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father. Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Bazzaz narrated it to us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad told us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Ibn Ajlan."
"1262","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, saying: Abu Ghassan told us, saying: Abd al-Salam told us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd — and he said:"
"1263","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated it to us from Abu Shihab, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us: ""When the ghouls appear to us in distorted forms, or when we see the ghoul, we call the adhan."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel. And we have heard it only from the hadith of Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd. And we do not know that al-Hasan heard anything from Sa'd."
"1264","What Ibn Umar narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd — the beginning of the Musnad of Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl: Ibn Umar from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Umar ibn Ali and Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Abu Ali al-Hanafi Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid told us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar told us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Sa'id ibn Zayd."
"1265","And al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Umar Abu al-Mundhir told us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar told us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Whoever takes a handspan of land without right shall be collared with it from seven earths"" — meaning on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith has been narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd through other channels, but we do not know it to be narrated from Ibn Umar, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, except through this channel."
"1266","What Amr ibn Hurayth narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: ""Truffles are of the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."" And it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels: Abu Hurayrah, Ibn Umar, Buraydah, and others narrated it. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd except from the hadith of Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id. And it has been narrated from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, by Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, al-Hasan al-Urani, and Salamah ibn Kuhayl."
"1267","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Truffles are of the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."""
"1268","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, saying: My father told me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Truffles are of the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."" Shu'bah said: And al-Hakam told me, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like thereof."
"1269","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, saying: Jarir told us, from Mutarrif, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Truffles are of the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."" As for the hadith of Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from al-Hasan al-Urani — we do not know anyone to have narrated it except Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from Shu'bah. As for the hadith of Mutarrif, from al-Hakam — Jarir and others narrated it."
"1270","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abu Ahmad told us, saying: Isra'il told us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from a man, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O people, praise Allah, since He has lifted the tithes (ushr) from you."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd except through this channel."
"1271","Among what Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman told us, from his father, from Abu Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd and Sa'id ibn Zayd, who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have not left after me any trial more harmful to men than women."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd except through this channel. Rather, this hadith is preserved from Abu Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd — so al-Mu'tamir joined them together, from his father, from Abu Uthman, from Usamah and Sa'id ibn Zayd."
"1272","Among what Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab told us, saying: Ayyub told us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever revives a dead land, it is his; and the unjust root has no right."" This hadith has been narrated by a group from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, as mursal. And we do not recall anyone to have said: from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, except Abd al-Wahhab, from Ayyub."
"1273","And Ubayd ibn Isma'il al-Habbari narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah told us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes a handspan of land without its right shall be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."" And it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by Abu Hurayrah through various routes, Ibn Umar, Ya'la ibn Murrah, and others."
"1274","Among what Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Umar told us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b told us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Whoever cuts off the wealth of a Muslim man by his oath, no blessing shall be in it for him. And whoever takes charge of a people without the permission of their masters, upon him is the curse of Allah — Allah shall accept from him neither sarf nor adl (no ransom nor recompense)."" And we do not know that Abu Salamah narrated, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, except this hadith."
"1275","Among what Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, saying: Rawh ibn Ubadah told us, saying: Salih, meaning Ibn Abi al-Akhdar, told us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."" Thus Salih narrated it. And Ibn Uyaynah narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd — without saying: from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl."
"1276","Among what Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us — the wording being that of Muhammad ibn Ziyad — saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah told us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr; and whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land shall be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."" And Ibrahim ibn Sa'd has narrated from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of: ""Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."""
"1277","Among what Abdullah ibn Zalim narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud told us, saying: Za'idah told us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abdullah ibn Zalim, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Killing suffices for my Companions."""
"1278","And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah told us, saying: Mis'ar told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abdullah ibn Zalim, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Killing suffices for my Companions."" As for the hadith of Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah — we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Abd al-Malik, with this chain, except Mis'ar. And we recall it only from the hadith of Abu Usamah, from Mis'ar."
"1279","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abdullah ibn Zalim, who said: I entered upon Sa'id ibn Zayd, and he said: Are you not amazed at this wrongdoer? He has set up preachers who revile Ali. He said: Have they done it? Or: Has he done it? I bear witness that nine are in Paradise. I said: Who are the nine? He said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Hira', and it shook — so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Be still, Hira' — there is upon you none but a prophet, a truthful one, and a martyr."" I said: And who was upon Hira'? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Sa'd, Talhah, al-Zubayr, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf were there. I said: Then who is the tenth? He said: I. This hadith has been narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd through other channels."
"1280","Among what Nawfal ibn Musahiq narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' told us, saying: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah told us, saying: Abdullah ibn Abi Husayn told us, from Nawfal ibn Musahiq, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among the worst of usury is a man's wilful aggression against his brother's honor."""
"1281","And Abdullah ibn Shabbuwayh narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman told us, saying: Shu'ayb told us, saying: Ibn Abi Husayn told us, from Nawfal ibn Musahiq, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The womb (kinship) is a branch from the Most Merciful: whoever cuts it, Allah shall forbid Paradise to him."" These two hadiths, we do not know them to be narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd except through this channel with this chain."
"1282","Among what Nufayl ibn Hisham narrated from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud told us, saying: al-Mas'udi told us. And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, saying: Abdullah ibn Raja' told us, saying: al-Mas'udi told us, saying: Nufayl ibn Hisham told us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — while Zayd ibn Harithah was with him — and they invited him to a meal-tray of theirs. So he said: ""O son of my brother, I do not eat of what is slaughtered upon stone altars."" He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen, after that day, eating of what was slaughtered upon stone altars. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'id except through this channel with this chain."
"1283","And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud told us, saying: al-Mas'udi told us, from Nufayl ibn Hisham, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: My father — as you have seen and as has reached you — had he met you, he would have believed in you; so seek forgiveness for him. So he said: ""Yes — for he shall come on the Day of Resurrection as a nation by himself."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd except through this channel, with this chain."
"1284","Among what Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, saying: I heard al-Hurr ibn Sayyah narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Ten of Quraysh are in Paradise: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is in Paradise, and Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman, and Sa'd"" — ""and the tenth of the Muslims — if I wished, I could name him"" — so we thought he meant himself. And we do not know that Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas narrated, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, except this hadith."
"1285","And al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated it to us, saying: My father told me, saying: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far told us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from al-Hurr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like thereof."
"1286","Among what al-Sha'bi narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, who said: I bear witness upon Sa'id ibn Zayd that he narrated: ""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a funeral procession, and he stood up."" This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Shu'bah, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi. And some of them said: I bear witness upon Sa'id; while some of them said: I bear witness upon Abu Sa'id. And we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd except through this channel."
"1287","Among what Amir ibn Sa'd al-Bajali narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Yusuf told us, saying: Sharik told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sa'd, meaning al-Bajali, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: When the news of the Negus's death came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Seek forgiveness for him."" This hadith has been narrated by some of them from Abu Ishaq, from al-Sha'bi. While Ishaq said: from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sa'd al-Bajali, from Sa'id ibn Zayd."
"1288","Among what Yuhannas narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, saying: Abu Nu'aym told us, saying: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb told us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Yuhannas, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Hasan: ""O Allah, I love him, so love him."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd except through this channel with this chain."
"1289","What Riyah ibn al-Harith narrated from Sa'id: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id told us, from Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna, from his grandfather Riyah ibn al-Harith, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Ten of Quraysh are in Paradise: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is in Paradise, and Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Uthman, and Ali, and Talhah, and al-Zubayr, and Sa'd, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf"" — ""and the tenth of the Muslims — if I wished, I could name him."" He said: So we thought he meant himself."
"1290","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Salamah told us, saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad told us, from Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna, from Riyah ibn al-Harith, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"1291","Among what the shaykhs narrated from Sa'id ibn Zayd: Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Khalid told us, saying: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym told us, from his father, from Qays ibn Abi Alqamah, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Lying upon me is not like lying upon anyone: whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."" In this hadith there are two defects: one is that Ibn Khuthaym — we do not know him to have narrated from his father except this hadith; and Qays ibn Abi Alqamah — we know of no mention of him except in this hadith."
"1292","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri told us, saying: Anas ibn Iyad told us, from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi', from Abd al-Karim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf ibn Sahl, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The neighbor has a right."""
"1293","The Musnad of Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — what Samurah ibn Jundub narrated from Abu Ubaydah: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id told us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Maymun told us, from Sa'd ibn Samurah, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah curse the Jews — they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."" And I think he said: ""Expel the Jews from the land of the Hijaz."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Ubaydah except through this channel with this chain."
"1294","Among what Abu Umamah narrated from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam told us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub told us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""The best of prayers is the dawn prayer on Friday in congregation; and I do not think any of you attends it but he is forgiven."" And we do not know anyone to have narrated these words except Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, with this chain."
"1295","Among what Abdullah ibn Suraqah narrated from Abu Ubaydah: Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abdullah ibn Suraqah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he mentioned the Dajjal and said: ""I shall describe him with a description no prophet before me has described: there was no prophet after Nuh but he warned his people of the Dajjal — and I warn you of him."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described him to us and said: ""Perhaps some of those who have seen me or heard my speech shall meet him."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall our hearts be that day? ""Like they are today — or better."" These words, we do not know for them any chain from Abu Ubaydah except this chain. And Shu'bah has narrated it from Khalid al-Hadhdha', with this chain — Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated it from him — except that Hammad ibn Salamah is more complete in wording."
"1296","Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abdullah ibn Suraqah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like thereof or close to it."
"1297","Among what Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani narrated from Abu Ubaydah: Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Hassan told us, saying: Yahya ibn Hamzah told us, from Abu Wahb, from Makhul, from Abu Tha'labah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The beginning of your religion is prophethood and mercy; then there shall be caliphate and mercy; then there shall be kingship and tyranny, in which blood shall be deemed lawful."""
"1298","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, saying: Jarir told us, from Layth, from Ibn Sabit, from Abu Tha'labah, from Abu Ubaydah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like thereof."
"1299","And Sulayman ibn Sayf al-Harrani narrated it to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud told us, saying: My father told me, from Makhul, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This affair shall ever remain standing until a man of Banu Umayyah breaches it."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain."
"1300","Among what Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb narrated from Abu Ubaydah: Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Himyar told me, saying: Abu al-Hasan told me, from Makhul, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which martyrs are most honored to Allah? He said: ""A man who stands up to an unjust ruler, enjoining him to good and forbidding him evil — so he kills him."" It was said: Then which people suffer the severest punishment? He said: ""A man who kills a prophet, or kills a man who enjoined him to good or forbade him evil."" Then he recited: {And they kill the prophets without right, and kill those who enjoin justice among the people — so give them tidings of a painful punishment}. Then he said: ""O Abu Ubaydah, the Children of Israel killed forty-three prophets in a single hour; then a hundred men and twelve men of the worshippers of the Children of Israel stood up, enjoining good and forbidding evil — and they were all killed."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this channel, from Abu Ubaydah. And we do not know for it any route from Abu Ubaydah other than this route. And I have not heard anyone name Abu al-Hasan, from whom Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated."
"1301","What al-Harith ibn Ghutayf narrated from Abu Ubaydah: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd told us, from Wasil, the freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Bashshar ibn Abi Sayf, from al-Harith ibn Ghutayf, who said: We visited Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah while he was ill, and at his head was his wife Tuhayfah. So we said: How did Abu Ubaydah spend the night? She said: He spent the night earning reward. So he raised his head and said: ""I did not spend the night earning reward."" So we fell silent. So he said: Why do you not ask me? So we said: Your speech has astonished us. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The illness of the believer is an expiation that removes his sins from him."" This hadith has also been narrated by Jarir ibn Hazim from Bashshar ibn Abi Sayf, from al-Harith ibn Ghutayf, from Abu Ubaydah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1302","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us with it, saying: Wahb ibn Jarir told us, saying: My father told me, from Bashshar ibn Abi Sayf, from al-Harith ibn Ghutayf, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like thereof."
"1303","Among what the uncle of Abd al-Rahman ibn Maslamah narrated from Abu Ubaydah: Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Khalid Sulayman ibn Hayyan told us, saying: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah told us, from al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maslamah, from his uncle, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Some of the Muslims grant protection on behalf of all of them."" This hadith, we do not know for it any route from Abu Ubaydah except this route. And Abd al-Rahman and his uncle — we do not know them to have narrated except this hadith."
"1304","Among what Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I heard a shaykh of the shaykhs of Basra narrating from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Haram ibn Uthman, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the house of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib and asked his wife Khawlah, saying: ""Where is Hamzah? Where is Abu Umarah?"" — or he said: ""Is Abu Umarah here?"" She said: No — and he has told me from you that you have a Hawd (fountain). He said: ""Yes — and the most beloved of those who shall come to it to me are your people."" These words have been narrated from Khawlah through another channel. And Haram ibn Uthman is weak in hadith; the scholars of transmission have refrained from transmitting his hadith due to the abundance of objectionable things he narrated — we only mentioned this hadith because we knew of no outlet for it."
"1305","The Musnad of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him — among what al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among what Ibn Abbas narrated from his father: Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi told us, saying: Rishdin ibn Kurayb told us, from his father, who said: I was leading Ibn Abbas in the alley of Abu Lahab — that was after his sight had gone — and he said: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""While a man is in his fine garments, looking at his shoulders, Allah causes him to sink — and he keeps sinking in them until the Day of Resurrection."" This hadith was narrated by al-Muharibi from Rishdin, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Abbas. And Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated it from Rishdin, from his father, from al-Abbas."
"1306","1291 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: al-Abbas said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, I have not seen anyone after Abu Bakr among the Quraysh who accepted Islam at Makkah on the day of the Conquest; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, grant Quraysh understanding in religion, and let them taste favor from this day of mine until the end of time, for You have let them taste punishment. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel with this chain; and Ibn Abbas narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through another channel."
"1307","1292 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad, nephew of Waki, Abu Ammar, narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to me, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Abdullah informed me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said: I took Abu Sufyan by the hand and brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a man who loves renown, so grant him something; so he said: Whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe, and whoever locks his door is safe. Then he stood, and I took his hand and seated him by the road, and the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began passing by him troop by troop; he would say: Who are these? And I would say: These are Muzaynah; so he would say: What have I to do with Muzaynah; there was no war between me and them in ignorance nor in Islam. Then a troop would pass, and he would say: Who are these? And I would say: These are Juhaynah, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed among the Emigrants; so when he saw them approaching, he turned to me and said: Your nephew has indeed been given a great kingdom, and he mentioned much speech therein. And this hadith was abridged from a long hadith, and this chain was in the middle of the hadith; and this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Abbas except through this channel with this connected chain."
"1308","1293 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, saying: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: al-Abbas said, I said: I do not know how long the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remaining among us; so I said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would take a trellis to shade you; he said: I shall remain among them, treading upon my heel and disputing my cloak, until Allah relieves me of them."
"1309","1294 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, who said: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said: I shall surely know how long the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remaining among us; then he mentioned similar to it, and he did not say from Ibn Abbas."
"1310","1295 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id, the seller of Tayalisah garments, narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Dashtaki narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Abi Qays informed us, saying: Simak narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from his father al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who said: We used to carry stones to the House when Quraysh built the House; men would carry stones, carrying two by two, and women would carry gypsum; and I and my nephew would carry, placing our garments under the stones, and when people approached us we covered ourselves with waist-wrappers. He said: While I was walking, with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ahead of me wearing nothing, Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lagged behind and fell flat upon his face; so I came hastening, cast down the two stones, while he was looking at something above him. I said: What is the matter with you? So he stood, took his waist-wrapper, and said: I was forbidden to walk naked. I said: Conceal it from people, fearing they would say mad. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Abbas except with this chain; and Amr ibn Abi Qays is upright in hadith, and a group of scholars narrated from him; and Amr ibn Abi Qays and Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated it from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas."
"1311","As for the hadith of Qays, Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, saying: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan informed us, saying: Qays informed us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1312","1297 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Isma'il al-Jabbuli narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I said to my father: O father, how did Abu al-Yasar capture you, when if you wished you could have held him in your hand? He said: O my son, do not say that, for he met me while he was greater in my eyes than al-Khandamah. And this hadith, we do not know a path for it from al-Abbas except this path."
"1313","1298 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Hakim narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Hashim Abu Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Sulayman ibn Urbayb, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of men - I think he said: the believer - is glad tidings from Allah, a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. He said: So I narrated it to Ibn Abbas, and he said: My father al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said what Abu Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: A part of forty-six parts of prophethood; so Ibn Abbas said, he said: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A part of fifty parts of prophethood."
"1314","1299 - Abdullah ibn Ziyad al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Abbas ibn Sahl saying: I would often sit with Ibn Abbas, and he narrated to me from his father al-Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I sit from the dawn prayer until the sun rises is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves from the children of Isma'il. And this hadith, only Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrates it from Ibn Abi Humayd, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl, from his father; and we do not know anyone who corroborated Ishaq in this narration."
"1315","1300 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar, from Arqam ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out while Abu Bakr was leading the people in prayer, and he recited from where Abu Bakr had reached. And we do not know these words narrated except through this channel with this chain."
"1316","And among what Kathir ibn al-Abbas narrated from him: 1301 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Kathir ibn al-Abbas narrated to me, from his father al-Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon his white mule on the day of Hunayn, and I was on one side and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith on the other side, holding its bridle; so the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: O Abbas, call the people, the companions of the Samurah tree; so al-Abbas called them, and he was a loud-voiced man; so when he called them, it was as though they were cattle turning to their young; then the voice rose: O company of the Ansar, then the call became exclusive: O sons of al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj; so he said: O companions of Surah al-Baqarah; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a handful of pebbles and said: Now the battle has grown fierce. And this hadith, similar words have been narrated through various channels from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and we do not know it narrated from al-Abbas except with this chain, from the hadith of Kathir ibn al-Abbas from his father, by the narration of al-Zuhri from Kathir; and we do not know Kathir ibn al-Abbas narrated from his father except this hadith."
"1317","And among what Tammam ibn al-Abbas narrated from his father: 1302 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Karran, a well-known Basran in whom there is no harm, narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Abbar narrated to us, saying: Mansur narrated to us, from Abu Ali al-Sayqal, from Ja'far ibn Tammam, from his father, from his grandfather al-Abbas, who said: They would enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without having used the tooth-stick, so he said: You enter upon me with yellow teeth; use the tooth-stick; and were it not that I would burden my community, I would have made the tooth-stick obligatory at every prayer, just as I made ablution obligatory upon them. And we do not know this wording narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from al-Abbas from him with this chain; and Tammam ibn al-Abbas narrated from his father another hadith."
"1318","And among what al-Ahnaf ibn Qays narrated from al-Abbas: 1303 - Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated to us, from Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has indeed cleared this peninsula of idolatry, so long as the stars do not lead them astray."
"1319","1304 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and we do not know for it a chain from al-Abbas except this chain."
"1320","1305 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Umar ibn Ibrahim, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from al-Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My community shall remain upon the natural disposition so long as they do not delay the Maghrib prayer until the interlacing of the stars."
"1321","1306 - And Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated it to us, saying: al-Awwam ibn Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from his father, from Umar ibn Ibrahim, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Abbas except through this channel; and we do not know any who narrated it except Umar ibn Ibrahim from Qatadah from al-Hasan; and more than one narrated it from Umar ibn Ibrahim, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Abbas, disconnected; and Ibrahim ibn Musa narrated it from Abbad ibn al-Awwam joined, and it was objected to him, so al-Awwam ibn Abbad was asked about that, and he produced it from the book of his father, as Ibrahim ibn Musa narrated it, joined."
"1322","1307 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abu Sa'id narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Dawud, peace be upon him, said: I ask You by the right of my forefathers Ibrahim and Ishaq and Ya'qub; so He said: As for Ibrahim, he was cast into the Fire and was patient for My sake, and that is a trial which did not reach you; and as for Ishaq, he offered himself for sacrifice and was patient for My sake, and that is a trial which did not reach you; and as for Ya'qub, Yusuf was taken away from him, and that is a trial which did not reach you. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except from the hadith of Abu Sa'id from Ali ibn Zayd; and this Abu Sa'id is al-Hasan ibn Dinar, and he is not strong in hadith; and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), disconnected, and he did not say from al-Abbas; and we mentioned this hadith, even though al-Hasan is pliant in hadith, only to clarify that he raised it, and that the hadith has a basis from the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1323","1308 - And Ma'mar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated to us, producing it to us from the original of his book, saying: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The sacrificed one is Ishaq. And this hadith, a group narrated it from al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from al-Abbas, halted."
"1324","1309 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Dashtaki narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Simak, from Abdullah ibn Umayrah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, may the mercy of Allah be upon him."
"1325","1310 - And Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated it to us, saying: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, saying: Simak narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umayrah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that he claimed he was sitting at al-Batha among a company, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting with them, when a cloud passed over them and they looked at it; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what this is called? They said: Yes, the cloud. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, and al-Muzn and al-Anan. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Do you know how far is the distance between heaven and earth? They said: No, by Allah, we do not know. He said: The distance between them is either one, or two, or seventy-three years; and the heaven which follows it is likewise; until he counted for them seven heavens likewise; then he said: Above the seventh is a sea, from its top to its bottom the distance between one heaven to another heaven; then above that are eight mountain goats, between their hooves and their knees the distance between one heaven to another heaven; and above their backs is the Throne, between its bottom and its top the distance between one heaven to another heaven; and Allah, blessed and exalted is He, is above that. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with these words and this wording except through this channel from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Abdullah ibn Umayrah, we do not know any who narrated from him except Simak ibn Harb, and Simak narrated from him other than one hadith."
"1326","And among what Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated from al-Abbas: 1311 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, blessings of Allah upon you, have you benefited Abu Talib with anything, for he used to grow angry for your sake and protect you? He said: Yes, he is in a shallow part of the Fire; and were it not for me, he would be in the lowest depth of the Fire. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except from the hadith of Abd al-Malik, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas; and it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels; Ibn Abbas, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, Abu Hurayrah and others narrated that; and the most eminent who narrated that is al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib."
"1327","1312 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, from Qays, meaning Ibn al-Rabi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas, may the mercy of Allah be upon him, who said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to say; he said: Ask Allah for pardon and well-being. And this hadith, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated it from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas, may the mercy of Allah be upon him; and we do not know any who narrated it from Abd al-Malik, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas, except Qays; and we heard it only from Ibrahim ibn Sa'id, from Abu Ahmad, from Qays."
"1328","1313 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra al-Dawsi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas, who said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, I wish to supplicate Allah, so teach me a supplication to supplicate with; he said: Ask Allah for well-being. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, joined to al-Abbas, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra."
"1329","1314 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, saying: Za'idah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to ask my Lord; he said: O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, ask Allah for well-being in this world and the Hereafter."
"1330","1315 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas, who said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, Quraysh, when they meet, greet one another cheerfully, but when they meet us, they meet us with faces we do not recognize. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew severely angry, then said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, faith shall not enter a heart until it loves you for Allah and His Messenger."
"1331","1316 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas, who said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, Quraysh sat and recalled their lineages, and made your likeness as a palm tree in a hollow of land; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted is He, created creation in two halves and placed me in the better of them; then He placed me in the better of the two parties; then He made the tribes and placed me in the best tribe; then He made the houses and placed me in the best of their houses; so I am the best of them in self and the best of them in house. And these two hadiths, we do not know any who narrated them except Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas."
"1332","Yazid ibn al-Asamm from al-Abbas: 1317 - Ali ibn Harb narrated to us, saying: Harun ibn Imran al-Mawsili narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who said: I saw in a dream as though the earth were being drawn up to heaven with strong ropes; so I related that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: That is the death of your nephew. And these words, we do not know them narrated except from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and we do not know for it a path except this path. End of the thirteenth part and beginning of the fourteenth, and praise be to Allah abundantly as He deserves."
"1333","And among what Amir ibn Sa'd narrated from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib: 1318 - Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from al-Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: He has tasted the flavor of faith who is pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Messenger. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib; and we do not know for it a path except this path."
"1334","1319 - And Muhammad ibn Uqbah narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hadi, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man is commanded to prostrate upon seven bones: his hands, his feet, his knees, and his face. And Sa'd, Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurayrah and others narrated it; and we do not know anyone who said bones except al-Abbas. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Abbas except through this channel with this chain; and Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father; and the correct one is the hadith of Amir ibn Sa'd from al-Abbas."
"1335","And among what Nafi ibn Jubayr narrated from al-Abbas: 1320 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, who said: I heard Nafi ibn Jubayr saying: al-Abbas said to al-Zubayr: Is it here that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded you to plant the banner? He only commanded you to plant it at Kada. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah from its upper part. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Abbas except through this channel with this chain."
"1336","And among what Muhammad ibn Ka'b narrated from al-Abbas: 1321 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Muhadir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sabrah, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from al-Abbas, who said: We sat with a people and they cut off their conversation; so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is the matter with people who converse, and when a man of my household sits with them, they cut off their conversation."
"1337","And among what Umm Kulthum bint al-Abbas narrated: 1322 - Muhammad ibn Uqbah narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Umm Kulthum bint al-Abbas, from her father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the skin of the servant shivers from fear of Allah, his sins fall from him as leaves fall from a withered tree. And these words, we do not preserve them with this wording from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from al-Abbas from him; and we do not know for it a chain from al-Abbas except this chain."
"1338","And among what the daughter of al-Hadi narrated from al-Abbas: 1323 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from the daughter of al-Hadi, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The religion shall surely prevail until it crosses the sea, and until seas are waded through with horses in the path of Allah; then there shall come a people who recite the Qur'an, saying: Who recites better than us? Who is more knowledgeable than us? Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned and said: Is there any good in those? They said: No. He said: Those are of this community; those are the fuel of the Fire."
"1339","1324 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah, from Aban ibn Salih, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from al-Abbas, that he said: One day I was in the mosque, and Abu Jahl came and said: Allah owes me that if I see Muhammad I shall tread upon his neck; so I went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until I entered upon him and informed him of the words of Abu Jahl; so he went out angry until he entered the mosque, and hastened to enter through the door, scaling the wall; so I said: A day of evil; and I hurried. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and recited: Read in the name of your Lord who created, created man from a clot, read and your Lord is Most Generous; and when he reached the part concerning Abu Jahl: Nay, man transgresses, because he sees himself self-sufficient; a man said to Abu Jahl: O Abu al-Hakam, this is Muhammad; so Abu Jahl said: Do you not see what I see? The horizon of heaven has been closed upon me. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached the end of the surah, he prostrated. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Abbas except through this channel with this chain."
"1340","And from the hadith of Ja'far ibn Abi Talib, what Amr ibn al-As narrated from Ja'far: 1325 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, saying: Ibn Awn narrated to us, saying: Umayr ibn Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Abi Talib said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to go to a land where I worship Allah fearing no one until I die. He said: So he permitted him, and he went to the Negus. And Mu'adh said: Ibn Awn narrated to me, saying: Umayr ibn Ishaq narrated to me, saying: Amr ibn al-As narrated to me, saying: When I saw Ja'far and his companions secure in the land of Abyssinia, I said: I shall surely attack this man and his companions; so I came to the Negus and said: Permit Amr ibn al-As; so he permitted me and I entered, and I said: In our land there is a cousin of this man who claims people have but one God; and by Allah, if you do not relieve us of him and his companions, neither I nor any of my companions shall ever bring you this semen-trade again. He said: Where is he? He said: He comes with your messenger; he does not come with me. So he sent a messenger with me, and we found him sitting among his companions; so he called him and he came; and when we reached the door, I called: Permit Amr ibn al-As, and he called behind me: Permit the party of Allah, mighty and majestic is He; so he heard his voice and permitted him, and he entered, and I entered; and the Negus was upon the couch, with Ja'far sitting before him and his companions around him upon cushions. And Umayr described the couch. Amr said: When I saw his seat, I came until I sat between him and the couch, placing him behind my back, and I seated between every two of his companions a man of my companions. He said: So he fell silent and we fell silent, and he fell silent and we fell silent, until I said to myself: Cursed be this Abyssinian slave, will he not speak. Then he spoke and said: Speak out. Amr said: meaning speak. So I said: The cousin of this man claims people have but one God; and by Allah, if you do not kill him, neither I nor any of my companions shall ever bring you this semen-trade again. So he said: O companions of Amr, what do you say? They said: We are upon what Amr said. So he said: O party of Allah, speak. He said: So Ja'far testified, and Amr said: By Allah, it was the first day I heard the testimony, that day. So he said: I testify there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He said: And you, what do you say? He said: I am upon his religion. He said: So he raised his hand and placed it upon his forehead, as Ibn Awn described, then said: A revelation like the revelation of Musa? What does he say concerning Isa? He said: He says: The spirit of Allah and His word. He said: So he took something from the ground, unerring, like this, and said: Were it not for my kingdom I would have followed you. Go, you O Amr; by Allah, I care not whether you or any of your companions ever come to me again. And go, you O party of Allah, for you are safe; whoever fights you I shall kill him, and whoever robs you I shall fine him. And he said to his chamberlain: Watch this man and do not veil him from me except when I am with my family; if I am with my family, inform him, and if he refuses but to be permitted, then permit him. He said: One evening I met him in the lane, and I looked behind him and saw no one behind him; so I took his hand and said: Do you know that I testify there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? He said: So he pinched me and said: Are you upon this; and we parted. And it was only that I came to my companions, and it was as though they had witnessed me and him; so they asked me nothing until they seized me and threw me down, placing a velvet cloth upon my face, pinching me, while I would free my head at times, until I slipped away naked with not a peel upon me, leaving me nothing but they took it. So I took a woman's veil from her head and placed it upon my private part; and she said to me so, and I said so, as though she marveled at me. He said: And I came to Ja'far and entered his house; and when he saw me he said: What is the matter with you? I said: It is only that I came to my companions, and it was as though they had witnessed me and you; so they asked me nothing until they cast a velvet cloth upon my face, smothering me with it, and took everything of this world that was mine; and you see upon me nothing but the veil of an Abyssinian woman which I took from her head. So he said: Go; and we reached the door of the Negus, and he called: Permit the party of Allah. And his chamberlain came and said: He is with his family. So he said: Ask permission for me; so he asked permission for him and he permitted him; and when he entered he said: Amr has left his religion and followed my religion. He said: No. He said: Yes. So he called his chamberlain and said: Go to Amr and say to him: This man claims you have left your religion and followed his religion. So I said: Yes. And my companions came to me until we stood at the door of the house; and I wrote down everything until I wrote down the handkerchief, leaving nothing taken but I seized it; and had I wished to take from their wealth, I would have done so. He said: Then afterwards I was among those who came in the ships as Muslims. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ja'far, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this wording except through this channel with this chain."
"1341","And among what Abu Musa narrated from Ja'far: 1326 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: News of the coming forth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached us, so we set out as emigrants until our ship cast us to the Negus in Abyssinia; and we found Ja'far ibn Abi Talib and his companions with the Negus; so Ja'far said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us here and commanded us to remain, so we remained with him until we all came together. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ja'far with a chain better than this nor more sound."
"1342","And among what Ibn Umar narrated from Ja'far: 1327 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, saying: A shaykh of Thaqif narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar, from Ja'far ibn Abi Talib: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to pray in the ship standing, so long as he does not fear drowning. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ja'far ibn Abi Talib except through this channel with this chain; and we do not know these words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) connected through any channel except through this channel. And we do not know for it a chain except this chain; and we do not know anyone who named the shaykh from whom Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated; and I saw some of our companions mentioning this hadith from Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ja'far; and I think he erred therein; it is in my view from Ibn Umar, as Ibn Dawud narrated it."
"1343","Abdullah ibn Ja'far from his father Ja'far: 1328 - Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Asad ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Mujalid ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Amir, meaning al-Sha'bi, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Talib, from his father, who said: When we came to the Negus, and wished to leave him, he loaded us, provisioned us and gave us, then said: Inform your companion of what I have done for you; and these are my messengers with you; and I testify there is no god but Allah and that he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so tell him: Seek forgiveness for me. Ja'far said: So we left him, and when we reached Madinah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me and embraced me, and said: I do not know whether I rejoice more at the conquest of Khaybar or at the arrival of Ja'far? Then he sat, and the messenger of the Negus stood and said: This is Ja'far, so ask him what our master did for him. So Ja'far said: He did for us, loaded us and provisioned us, and testified there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah, and said: Tell him to seek forgiveness for me. So he supplicated three times, saying: O Allah, forgive the Negus. And the Muslims said: Amen. Ja'far said: So I said to the messenger: Go and convey to your master what you saw of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ja'far connected except from the hadith of Asad ibn Amr, from Mujalid, with this chain."
"1344","1329 - And al-Ajlah narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi, who said: When Ja'far came from Abyssinia, and he did not mention therein from Abdullah ibn Ja'far. Thus Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated it to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from al-Sha'bi."
"1345","1330 - And Yahya ibn Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated it to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Yahya ibn Hani narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: al-Ajlah narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ja'far; and he mentioned the story of Ja'far, with its chain."
"1346","Musnad of Zayd ibn Harithah, may Allah be pleased with him; beginning of the musnad of Zayd ibn Harithah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Usamah from his father: 1331 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah and Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father Zayd ibn Harithah, who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with him seating me behind him, on a hot day of the days of Makkah; and with us was a sheep we had slaughtered and prepared, placing it in a travel meal-bag; and Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl met him, and each greeted the other with the greeting of ignorance. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Zayd, meaning Zayd ibn Amr, why do I see your people have turned away from you? He said: By Allah, O Muhammad, that is for no offense of mine against them; but I went out seeking this religion until I came to the rabbis of Khaybar and found them worshipping Allah yet associating with Him; so I said: This is not the religion I seek. So I went out until I came to the rabbis of Syria, and found them worshipping Allah yet associating with Him; so I said: This is not the religion I seek. So a man of them said: You ask about a religion which we know none worships Allah with except an elder in al-Jazirah. So I went out until I came to him; and when he saw me he said: All whom you have seen are in error; so whence are you? I said: I am of the people of the House of Allah, of the people of idolatry and qaraz. He said: What you seek has appeared in your land; a prophet has been sent whose star has risen; and I have sensed nothing yet, O Muhammad. He said: So he offered him the meal-bag, and he said: What is this? He said: A sheep we slaughtered for one of these sacrificial stones. He said: I would never eat anything slaughtered for other than Allah; and they parted. Zayd ibn Harithah said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the House, with me, and circumambulated it; and at the House were two idols, one of brass, called one of them Yasaf and the other Na'ilah; and the idolaters, when they circumambulated, would wipe them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wipe them, for they are filth. He said: So I said to myself: I shall surely wipe them to see what he says; so I wiped them, and he said: O Zayd, were you not forbidden? He said: And revelation descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And Zayd ibn Amr died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He shall be raised as a community alone. And this hadith, we do not know any who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Zayd ibn Harithah with this chain."
"1347","1332 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, saying: al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Harithah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), at the first of what was revealed to him, Jibril came to him and taught him ablution; and when he finished, he took a handful of water and sprinkled his private part with it."
"1348","And among what al-Bara narrated from Zayd ibn Harithah: 1333 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from al-Bara, from Zayd ibn Harithah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you made brotherhood between me and Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Zayd ibn Harithah except through this channel with this chain."
"1349","And among what Abu al-Tufayl narrated from Zayd ibn Harithah: 1334 - Muhammad ibn Amir al-Antaki narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, saying: Ziyad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Furat al-Qazzaz, from Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah, from Zayd ibn Harithah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to one of his companions: Go forth; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went forth with his companions until they entered between two walls in a long lane; and when they reached the house, there was a woman sitting, and a great water-skin full of water; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see a water-skin but see no bearer. So the woman pointed to a velvet cloth in a corner of the house; so they went to the cloth and uncovered it, and beneath it was a man; so he raised his head, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May the face be deformed. So he said: O Muhammad, why do you revile me? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I have concealed for you something hidden; tell me what it is. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had concealed for him Surah al-Dukhan; so he said: Al-Dukhk. So he said: Be gone; whatever Allah wills shall be. Then he departed. And this hadith, part of it Abu al-Tufayl himself narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and none mentioned it with this chain from Zayd ibn Harithah."
"1350","Beginning of the musnad of al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: 1335 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, saying: Hubayrah ibn Hudayr al-Adawi narrated to us, saying: Sa'd al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Umayr ibn al-Ma'mum, who said: I came to Madinah visiting a cousin of mine married to al-Hasan ibn Ali; and I witnessed with him the dawn prayer in the mosque of the Messenger, while Ibn al-Zubayr had prepared a feast in the morning. So the messenger of Ibn al-Zubayr came and said: O son of the Messenger of Allah, Ibn al-Zubayr has prepared a feast in the morning and sent me to you; but he paid no attention to him. So he roamed the mosque, parting the people to invite them, then returned to al-Hasan and said: O son of the Messenger of Allah, Ibn al-Zubayr has prepared a feast and sent me to you. So he turned to me and said: Has the sun risen? It was said: No, I think it has risen. So he said: Praise be to Allah who raised it from its rising-place. Then he said: I heard my father and my grandfather, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Whoever prays the dawn prayer then sits remembering Allah until the sun rises, Allah shall place between him and the Fire a veil. Then he said: Rise and answer Ibn al-Zubayr. And when we reached the door, Ibn al-Zubayr met him at the door and said: O son of the Messenger of Allah, you were late to me this day. So he said: I have answered you, though I am fasting. Then he said: So here is a gift. So al-Hasan ibn Ali said: I heard my father and my grandfather, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The gift for the fasting visitor is that his beard be perfumed, his clothes fumigated and sprinkled with scent; and the gift for the fasting woman visitor is that her head be combed, her clothes fumigated and sprinkled with scent. He said: I said, O son of the Messenger of Allah, repeat the hadith to me. He said: I heard my father and my grandfather, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Whoever frequents the mosque shall attain a decisive verse, or an awaited mercy, or fresh knowledge, or a word increasing him in guidance or turning him from ruin, or he leaves sins out of fear or shame. And these words, we do not preserve them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel; and Sa'd al-Hadhdha is Sa'd ibn Tarif; and Umayr ibn al-Ma'mum, we do not know any who narrated from him except Sa'd."
"1351","1336 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, saying: Burayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu al-Hawra, who said: I said to al-Hasan ibn Ali: What do you remember of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I took a date from the dates of charity and cast it into my mouth; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed it and cast it among the dates; and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, you took a date from this boy. He said: We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us; or he said: We do not eat charity. And he would say: Leave what puts you in doubt for what does not put you in doubt; for truthfulness is tranquility, and lying is doubt. And he would teach us this supplication: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, befriend me among those You befriended, bless for me what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed none whom You befriend is humbled; blessed and exalted are You. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except al-Hasan ibn Ali."
"1352","1337 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra al-Sa'di, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to say in the qunut of witr: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend me among those You befriended, bless for me what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed none whom You befriend is humbled; blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted. And this hadith, we do not know any who narrates it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Hasan ibn Ali. And Shu'bah narrated it from Burayd, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, while Abu Ishaq added, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to say in the qunut of witr; and Shu'bah did not say in the qunut of witr; therefore we wrote it; and the name of Abu al-Hawra is Rabi'ah ibn Shayban."
"1353","1338 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Ibn Idris narrated to us, saying: Thabit ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Shayban, who said: I said to al-Hasan: Do you preserve anything of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He admitted me to a room, and I took a date of charity dates; so he said: It is not lawful for Muhammad, nor for anyone of his household. And this hadith, it has been narrated from Burayd, narrated by more than one with differing wordings; and Thabit ibn Umarah came, from Rabi'ah ibn Shayban, who is Abu al-Hawra, with a wording contrary to the wording of Shu'bah; so we mentioned it for that, intending to clarify that Abu al-Hawra was narrated from by other than Burayd; therefore we wrote it."
"1354","1339 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Hubayrah, who said: al-Hasan ibn Ali addressed us, saying: By Allah, tonight a man was killed whom neither the first nor the last shall surpass; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send him in expeditions, with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left; and by Allah, he left neither yellow nor white. And these words, we do not know anyone who mentions them other than al-Hasan ibn Ali; and it has another chain from al-Hasan with an added wording which we shall mention, Allah willing, due to the addition therein."
"1355","1340 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, saying: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Khalid narrated to me, saying: My father Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to me, saying: When Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, al-Hasan ibn Ali stood as orator and said: By Allah, tonight you have killed a man, in the night in which the Qur'an was sent down, in which Isa son of Maryam was raised, and in which Yusha ibn Nun, the youth of Musa, was killed. Sukayn said: A man he named narrated to me, saying: And therein repentance was accepted for the children of Isra'il. Then he returned to the hadith of Hafs ibn Khalid, saying: By Allah, none before him surpassed him, nor shall any after him reach him; and by Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send him in expeditions, with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left; and by Allah, he left neither yellow nor white except eight hundred dirhams, or seven hundred dirhams, which he had prepared for a servant. And this hadith with these wordings, we do not know anyone who narrates them except al-Hasan ibn Ali with this chain; and its chain is sound; and we do not know any who narrates from Hafs ibn Khalid except Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"1356","1341 - Abu Ja'far Ahmad ibn Musa al-Tamimi narrated to us, saying: al-Qasim ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salim narrated to us, from Abu al-Jarud, from Mansur, from Abu Razin, who said: al-Hasan ibn Ali addressed us when his father was struck, wearing a black turban, saying: O people, last night a man parted from you whom neither the first nor the last shall surpass; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send him on missions and give him the banner; and when he scented battle, meaning war, and fought, Jibril fought on his right and Mika'il on his left, and he would not return until Allah granted him victory. He has passed, leaving neither yellow nor white except seven hundred dirhams remaining of his stipend, intending to buy a servant for his household therewith. And he died in the night in which Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon him, died, and in the night in which Yusha ibn Nun, the youth of Musa, peace be upon him, was taken; and it was the twenty-first of Ramadan. And we do not know Abu Razin narrated from al-Hasan ibn Ali except this hadith."
"1357","Musnad of al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both; beginning of the musnad of al-Husayn ibn Ali from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 1342 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar said: Abu Amir narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Husayn, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The miser is he in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me."
"1358","1343 - Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir narrated to us, saying: Sulayman narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Muhammad, from Ya'la ibn Abi Yahya, from Ali ibn Husayn, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The beggar has a right, even if he comes upon a horse."
"1359","1344 - Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Abu Idris, from al-Musayyab ibn Najabah, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: War is deceit."
"1360","1345 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Jahhaf and Isma'il ibn Raja; he said: And Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salim ibn Abi Hafsah, from Abu Hazim, who said: When al-Hasan ibn Ali died, al-Husayn said to Sa'id ibn al-As, who was the governor of Madinah: Step forward; were it not a practice, you would not be advanced."
"1361","Musnad of Bilal ibn Rabah, may Allah be pleased with him; what Ibn Umar narrated from Bilal; beginning of the musnad of Bilal from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); what Ibn Umar narrated from Bilal: 1346 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from al-Sa'ib ibn Umar, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Umar, who said: I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray when he entered the Ka'bah? He said: Between the two pillars. And this hadith, other than al-Sa'ib narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Umar."
"1362","1347 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, saying: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, saying: Isra'il narrated to us, saying: Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out walking between Usamah ibn Zayd and Bilal, until he entered the Ka'bah, wherein was a beam laid across. And when Usamah ibn Zayd came out, I asked him: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do? He said: He left a third of the beam on his right and prayed in the remaining third on its left. I said: How many did he pray? He said: And I did not ask Bilal."
"1363","1348 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in the House? He said: Between the two columns. And we do not know any who narrated the hadith of al-A'mash from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, except Amr ibn Thabit; and we heard it only from Muhammad ibn Marzuq."
"1364","1349 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from Salim and Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah, with him Uthman ibn Shaybah and Bilal; so I crowded until I reached the door, and found him already out; so I asked them both: What did he do? They said: He prayed two units between the two columns. And Ayyub, Ubaydullah, Ibn Awn, Isma'il ibn Umayyah, Uthman ibn Murrah and others narrated it from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal."
"1365","1350 - As for the hadith of Ubaydullah, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, saying: Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah, he with Uthman ibn Talhah, Usamah ibn Zayd and Bilal. He said: So I remained, and he tarried long, then came out; and I was the first of people to enter after him; and Bilal was at the House; so I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two front columns."
"1366","1351 - As for the hadith of Ibn Awn, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, saying: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal, similar to the hadith of Ubaydullah."
"1367","1352 - And Bishr ibn Khalid narrated it to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal, similar to the hadith of Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal."
"1368","1353 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Quba, and the Ansar came greeting him while he was praying; so I said to Bilal: How would he return their greeting while praying? He said: He would say thus with his hand."
"1369","1354 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1370","1355 - And Yusuf ibn Wadih narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Habib narrated to us, saying: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, from Bilal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Nafi."
"1371","And among what Jabir narrated from Bilal: 1356 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, saying: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Sayyar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from Bilal, who said: I called the adhan on a cold morning, and people were slow to come to prayer; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with the people, O Bilal? I said: The cold detained them. So he said: O Allah, remove the cold from them. He said: So I saw them finding cool relief in the dawn prayer. And this hadith, we do not know any who narrated it from Ibn al-Munkadir except Ayyub ibn Sayyar, and he was not corroborated in it; and Ayyub is not strong; and a group of scholars narrated from him."
"1372","And Ayyub ibn Sayyar narrated from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from Abu Bakr, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray the dawn at full light, for it is greater in reward. 1357 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated it to us, saying: Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Sayyar narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from Abu Bakr, from Bilal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so I did not begin with this hadith at the start of the musnad of Bilal due to the weakness of Ayyub ibn Sayyar."
"1373","Ka'b ibn Ujrah from Bilal: 1358 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah and Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from Bilal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the leather socks; I think he said: and the head-cover. And we do not know Ka'b ibn Ujrah narrated from Bilal other than this hadith."
"1374","Al-Bara from Bilal: 1359 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Za'idah, meaning Ibn Qudamah, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, from Bilal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1375","1360 - And al-Abbas ibn Ja'far narrated it to us, saying: Abu al-Jawwab al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, saying: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara, from Bilal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the leather socks and the head-cover. And we do not know al-Bara narrated from Bilal other than this hadith."
"1376","And among what Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab narrated from Bilal: 1361 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim and al-Fadl ibn Sahl said: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, saying: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Bilal: that they slept with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey until the sun rose; so when they stood, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal, and he called the adhan, then prayed two units, then Bilal called the iqamah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in prayer after the sun had risen. And this hadith, other than Abd al-Samad narrated it from Abu Ja'far, from Yahya, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, disconnected."
"1377","1362 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hamzah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Bilal, who said: I had dates and sold them in the market for better dates at half their measure; so I offered them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I have not seen today dates better than these; whence is this, O Bilal? So I told him what I had done, and he said: Go and return it to its owner, take your dates, sell them for wheat or barley, then buy of these dates therewith. So I did. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dates for dates, like for like; wheat for wheat, like for like; barley for barley, like for like; salt for salt, like for like; gold for gold, like for like; silver for silver, weight for weight; and whatever is in excess is usury."
"1378","1363 - And this hadith, Qays narrated it from Abu Hamzah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated it to us, saying: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated; and there has been narrated concerning the story of the dates, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, with other than this wording; so they differed over Sa'id: Qatadah said, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Sa'id; and Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl said, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id."
"1379","Aslam, freedman of Umar, from Bilal: 1364 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: al-Walid ibn Ata ibn al-Agharr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Mus'ab narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that Bilal said: When this verse was revealed: Their sides forsake their beds, the verse, we would sit in the gathering while some of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed after Maghrib until Isha; so this verse was revealed: Their sides forsake their beds. And we do not know Aslam narrated from Bilal except this hadith; and we do not know for it a path from Bilal other than this path."
"1380","And among what Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb narrated from Bilal: 1365 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, who said: Nimran, meaning Ibn Ubaydullah, informed me that Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb narrated to him from Bilal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The callers to prayer shall have the longest necks of people on the Day of Resurrection. And we do not know Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb narrated from Bilal other than this hadith; and we do not know for it a chain except this chain."
"1381","And among what Masruq ibn al-Ajda narrated from Bilal: 1366 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, from Bilal, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in, with him a heap of wealth, and said: Spend, O Bilal, and fear no decrease from the Lord of the Throne. And this hadith, other than Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated it from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to Bilal, without joining its chain; and none joined its chain except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan; and Yahya ibn Waththab narrated it from Masruq, from Abdullah."
"1382","1367 - And al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Razin narrated to us, saying: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, from Bilal, who said: I had dates and sold them for better, at half their measure or part of their measure; so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him what I had done; so he said: Go, return it to its owner and take your dates; dates for dates, like for like. So I did. And this hadith, Amr ibn Muhammad and Uthman ibn Umar narrated it from Isra'il."
"1383","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Bilal: 1368 - Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisi narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wipe over the leather socks and the head-cover. And we do not know Mansur narrated from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, except this hadith; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mansur except Za'idah."
"1384","1369 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Masruqi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Muhayyah Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Layth, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the leather socks; and after him Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, wiped."
"1385","1370 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal."
"1386","1371 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Ziyad ibn Abdullah informed us, saying: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death of anyone, nor for his life; rather they are two signs of the signs of Allah; so when you see that, pray as the most recent prayer you prayed. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Bilal except through this channel with this chain; and we heard it only from Nasr; and other than Nasr said, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, saying: So-and-so narrated to me, while Nasr named him, saying: from Bilal."
"1387","1372 - Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, saying: Abu Mas'ud Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Zajjaj narrated to us, saying: Abu Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to make the second call in the dawn prayer. And this hadith, we do not know any who narrated it from Abu Sa'd except Abu Mas'ud al-Zajjaj."
"1388","1373 - And Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: Abu Isra'il al-Mula'i narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to make the second call in the dawn prayer, and not to make it in the Maghrib prayer. And this hadith, we do not know any who narrated it from al-Hakam except Abu Isra'il."
"1389","And among what Shaddad, freedman of Iyad, narrated from Bilal: 1374 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Waki narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Shaddad, freedman of Iyad, from Bilal: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call the adhan until the dawn appears distinct like this; and he stretched his hands wide."
"1390","And among what Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated from Bilal: 1375 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab narrated to us, saying: al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Asim, meaning al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Bilal, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not precede me with Amen. And this hadith, more than one narrated it without joining its chain, and more than one narrated it joining its chain; and we do not know Abu Uthman narrated from Bilal other than this hadith."
"1391","And among what al-Sunabihi narrated from Bilal: 1376 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from al-Sunabihi, from Bilal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-fourth. And we do not know al-Sunabihi narrated from Bilal except this hadith; and we do not know for it a path except this path."
"1392","And among what Abu Idris narrated from Bilal: 1377 - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Idris, from Bilal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the leather socks and the head-cover."
"1393","1378 - al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Rashid narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us, from Humayd, from Abu Raja, freedman of Abu Qilabah, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Idris, from Bilal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the leather socks and the head-cover. And the hadith of Ayyub, more than one narrated it from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Bilal, without mentioning Abu Idris; and we do not know anyone who said from Abu Idris except Hammad ibn Salamah; and none said from Abu Raja, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Idris, except Khalid; and Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated it from Humayd, from Abu Raja, from Abu Idris, from Bilal, without mentioning Abu Qilabah; and Abu Raja, freedman of Abu Qilabah, is well-known, Humayd and al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated from him; and al-Mu'tamir narrated this hadith from Humayd, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, erring therein."
"1394","And among what Abu Jandal narrated from Bilal: 1379 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Amir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Jandal ibn Suhayl ibn Amr, from Bilal, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the leather socks and the head-cover. And we do not know any who narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Umar ibn Amir."
"1395","1380 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Abu Wahb, from Makhul, from al-Harith ibn Mu'awiyah and Abu Jandal, from Bilal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the leather socks and the head-cover. And it has been narrated from Makhul, from Abu Jandal, and from al-Harith ibn Mu'awiyah through other channels; so we sufficed with what we mentioned."
"1396","And among what Abu Za'idah Ubaydullah ibn Za'idah al-Kindi narrated from Bilal: 1381 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Ala narrated to us, saying: Abu Za'idah Ubaydullah ibn Za'idah narrated to us, from Bilal, that he narrated to him that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to announce the dawn prayer, but A'ishah detained Bilal until the morning exposed him plainly; so it became fully morning, and Bilal stood and called the adhan, announcing the prayer with his adhan, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not come out. And when he came out to lead the people in prayer, he informed him that A'ishah had detained him for a matter she asked him about until it became fully morning, and that he was late in coming out; so he said: I prayed the two units of dawn. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, it has become morning. So he said: Had it become morning, then morning again, I would have prayed them, perfecting and beautifying them."
"1397","And among what Abdullah al-Hawzani narrated from Bilal: 1382 - al-Fudayl ibn Abdullah and Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tamimi said: al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam saying: Abdullah al-Hawzani narrated to me, saying: I met Bilal, the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Bilal, tell me how was the expenditure of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had nothing; I was the one who would borrow for him from when Allah sent him until he died. When a Muslim man would come to him and he saw him bare, he would command me, and I would borrow for him, clothing and feeding him; until a man of the idolaters said to me: O Bilal, I have means, so borrow from none but me. So I did. One day I performed ablution then went out to prayer, and the idolater was among a company of merchants; when he saw me he said to me: Do you know how long between you and the month you promised to repay me? I said: Soon. He said: Between you and it are but four; so I shall seize you for the debt owed me; for I gave you what I gave not out of honor for you nor honor for your companion; I gave you only that a debt be established against you, returning you to herding sheep as you were. So my soul felt what souls feel. So I set out and called the prayer; and when I prayed the night prayer and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to his family, I asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The idolater from whom I borrowed has come threatening me; and neither you have wherewith to repay, nor I; and he is due; so permit me to go to some of these tribes who have accepted Islam until Allah provides His Messenger wherewith to repay for me. So I went out to my house, placing my sword, bag and sandals at my head, facing the horizon; and I said: When I see the light of dawn I shall call; and when dawn broke I wished to set out, so I called; and a man came hastening calling me, saying: O Bilal, answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I went until I reached him, and four kneeling camels with their loads upon them; so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked permission; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Rejoice, for Allah has brought repayment of the debt. So I praised Allah. And he said: Do you not see the four kneeling camels? I said: Yes. He said: They with what is upon them are yours; upon them are clothing and food gifted to me by the chief of Fadak; so take them and repay your debt. He said: So I unloaded their saddles, then prayed the dawn prayer; and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, I went out to al-Baqi, placing my fingers in my ears, saying: Whoever seeks a debt, let him attend. And I kept selling and repaying until no debt of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to anyone remained, with two ounces or an ounce and a half remaining in my hand. Then I went to the mosque and found most of the day gone, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing in the mosque; so I greeted him, and he said: What happened to what was with you? I said: Allah has settled everything owed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); nothing remains. He said: Did anything remain? I said: Yes. He said: See that you relieve me of it, for I shall not enter upon any of my family until you relieve me of it. And none came to us until evening; and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the night prayer, he called me and said: What happened to what was with you? I said: It is with me; none came to us. So the Messenger of Allah stood until morning, remaining in the mosque until the second day; then two men came, and I took them, feeding and clothing them; and when he prayed the night prayer, he called me and said: What happened to what was with you? I said: Allah has relieved you of it, O Messenger of Allah. So he praised Allah for that, then went to his wives, greeting each wife. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain."
"1398","Musnad of Ammar ibn Yasir, may Allah be pleased with him; beginning of the musnad of Ammar ibn Yasir: 1383 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Ibrahim said: And Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq. 1384 - And Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated it to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, all closely agreeing in their hadith; he mentioned it from Ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Ammar, who said: I was among the people until the concession of wiping with dust was revealed when we find no water; so he commanded us, and we struck once for the face, then struck another for the hands to the elbows; and in the hadith of Ahmad ibn Khalid he said: To the shoulders, front and back. And this hadith, more than one narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Ammar, corroborating Ibn Ishaq; and more than one narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, without saying from Ibn Abbas, from Ammar. And some companions of al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from his father, from Ammar, with other than this wording."
"1399","And among what Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza narrated from Ammar: 1385 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father: that a man came to Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, saying: I became ritually impure and found no water. So Umar said: Do not pray. So Ammar said: Do you not remember, O Commander of the Faithful, when you and I were in an expedition and became ritually impure and found no water; as for you, you did not pray, while I rolled in the dust and prayed. And when we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I mentioned that to him, and he said: It would have sufficed you; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the earth with his hand, then blew, and wiped therewith his face and hands."
"1400","1386 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, who said: A man came to Umar asking him about one ritually impure who finds no water. He said: He does not pray until he finds water. So Ammar said: Do you not remember, O Commander of the Faithful, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent you and me to such-and-such place, and I became ritually impure and rolled in the earth; and I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It would have sufficed you so-and-so; and he placed his hands in the earth and wiped therewith his hands and face. And this hadith, other than al-A'mash narrated it from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Malik, from Ammar."
"1401","1387 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, saying: Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ammar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1402","1388 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Ammar, without mentioning Azrah."
"1403","1389 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ammar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said concerning dry ablution: One strike for the face and the hands."
"1404","1390 - Ibrahim said: I heard Musa ibn Isma'il saying: Aban narrated to us, saying: Qatadah was asked about dry ablution in travel, and he said: Ibn Umar would say: To the elbows; and al-Hasan and Ibrahim would say: To the elbows."
"1405","1391 - He said: And a narrator narrated to me from al-Sha'bi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To the elbows. And he mentioned the hadith of Qatadah, from Azrah, as Affan narrated it; he said: Ibrahim ibn Hani said: So I mentioned it to Ahmad ibn Hanbal, and he marveled at it."
"1406","And among what Qays ibn Abbad narrated from Ammar: 1392 - Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My uncle narrated to me, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Hashim; and he said: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: Sharik narrated to me, from Abu Hashim, from Abu Mijlaz, from Qays ibn Abbad, who said: Ammar ibn Yasir prayed a prayer, lightening it; so a man said to him: You lightened it. He said: Did I not complete the bowing and prostration? He said: Yes. He said: Yet I supplicated therein with supplications, or a supplication, I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Allah, by Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over creation, keep me alive so long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me; and I ask You fear of You in secret and openly, and I ask You the word of truth in anger and pleasure, and I ask You moderation in poverty and wealth, and I ask You bliss that perishes not, and coolness of eye that ceases not, and I ask You contentment after decree, and I ask You coolness of life after death, and I ask You the gaze upon Your Face, and I ask You longing to meet You, without harmful adversity nor misleading trial. And we do not know Qays ibn Abbad narrated from Ammar except this hadith."
"1407","And among what al-Sa'ib ibn Malik narrated from Ammar: 1393 - Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father: that Ammar prayed with his companions one day, shortening it; so it was said to him: O Abu al-Yaqzan, you shortened it. He said: Yet therewith I supplicated with supplications I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And when he stood, I followed him, or a man stood and followed him, asking him, then came informing the people, saying: O Allah, by Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over creation, keep me alive so long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me; and I ask You fear of You in secret and openly, and I ask You the word of truth in anger and pleasure, and I ask You moderation in poverty and wealth, and I ask You bliss that perishes not, and coolness of eye that ceases not, and I ask You contentment after decree, and I ask You coolness of life after death, and I ask You the delight of gazing upon Your Face, and I ask You longing to meet You, without harmful adversity nor misleading trial."
"1408","Silah ibn Zufar from Ammar: 1394 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, saying: Abu Khalid, meaning Sulayman ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah, who said: We were with Ammar, meaning on the day doubted of Ramadan, when a roasted sheep was brought; so he said: Eat. And some of the people withdrew, saying: I am fasting. So Ammar said: Whoever fasts the day doubted of has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know any who narrated it from Amr ibn Qays except Abu Khalid."
"1409","1395 - And Fadalah ibn al-Fadl al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah, meaning Ibn Zufar, from Ammar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give greeting to his right and left in prayer. And this hadith, Shu'bah narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ammar, halted; and we do not know anyone who said from Silah, from Ammar, except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"1410","1396 - al-Hasan ibn Abdullah al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah, from Ammar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three are of faith: spending from scant means, offering greeting to the world, and fairness from oneself. And this hadith, more than one narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Silah, from Ammar, halted; and this shaykh joined its chain, from Abd al-Razzaq."
"1411","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Ammar: 1397 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, saying: Thabit ibn Hammad narrated to us, and he was trustworthy, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ammar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was at a well drawing water in a vessel of mine, and said: What are you doing? So I said, O Messenger of Allah, I am washing my garment of impurity that befell it. So he said: O Ammar, the garment is washed only of excrement, urine, vomit and blood. And this hadith, none narrated it except Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya, from Thabit ibn Hammad; and Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya is a Basran who narrated other than one hadith uncorroborated; and as for Thabit ibn Hammad, we do not know he narrated except this hadith."
"1412","And among what Maymun ibn Abi Shabib narrated from Ammar: 1398 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, saying: Firdaws ibn al-Ash'ari narrated to us, saying: Mas'ud ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The length of a man's prayer and shortness of his sermon are a sign of a man's understanding; so lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermons. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Of eloquence is surely magic. And this hadith, we do not know any who narrated it from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun, from Ammar, except Mas'ud ibn Sulayman; and Mas'ud ibn Sulayman, we do not know anyone who said Mas'ud except Firdaws; and other than Firdaws narrated some of the hadiths of Firdaws, from Sa'ad ibn Sulayman, and he is one: Sa'ad and Mas'ud."
"1413","1399 - Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Absi narrated to us, saying: Mahbub ibn Muhriz narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man strikes a slave of his but retribution shall be taken from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1414","1400 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us; Qays narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Ammar, similar to it, without raising it."
"1415","And among what Ibn Hubaysh narrated from Ammar: 1401 - al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, meaning Ibn Hubaysh, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsah, Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: Take back Hafsah, for she is fasting, praying at night; and she is your wife in Paradise. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ammar except through this channel with this chain."
"1416","And among what Yahya ibn Ya'mar narrated from Ammar: 1402 - Abdullah ibn Abi Thumamah al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, saying: Ata al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: I came to my family at night from a journey, my hands having cracked; so they perfumed me with saffron. So I went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him, but he did not return my greeting nor welcome me, saying: Wash this off you. So I went and washed it, then returned to him, greeting him; and he welcomed me, saying: The angels do not attend the funeral of a disbeliever, nor one smeared with saffron."
"1417","And among what Abdullah ibn Utbah narrated from Ammar: 1403 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from his father, from Ammar, who said: We performed dry ablution with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the shoulders and armpits. And we do not know Abdullah ibn Utbah narrated from Ammar except this hadith."
"1418","And among what Muhammad ibn Ammar narrated from his father: 1404 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah al-Awsi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sakhr, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar, from his father, from Ammar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ammar except with this chain; and we do not know any who narrated from Isma'il ibn Sakhr except Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir."
"1419","1405 - And Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, saying: Salamah ibn Ubaydullah al-Rahawi narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said: Amen, amen, amen. And when he descended, he was asked; so he said: Jibril came to me and said: May the nose of a man who reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven be rubbed in dust, or may Allah distance him; say: Amen. So I said: Amen. And may the nose of a man who reaches his parents and they do not admit him to Paradise be rubbed in dust, or may Allah distance him; say: Amen. So I said: Amen. And a man in whose presence you are mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon you, may Allah distance him; say: Amen. So I said: Amen. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ammar except through this channel with this chain."
"1420","And among what Abu Wa'il narrated from Ammar: 1406 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Wasil ibn Hayyan, who said: Abu Wa'il narrated to us, saying: Ammar ibn Yasir addressed us, eloquent and brief; so we said: O Abu al-Yaqzan, you were eloquent and brief. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The length of prayer and shortness of sermons are a sign of a man's understanding; so lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermons."
"1421","1407 - And Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated it to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar, I think, from Wasil, from Abu Wa'il, from Ammar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1422","1408 - Muhammad ibn Salim al-Bahili narrated to us, saying: Abu Attab Sahl ibn Hammad narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Wa'il, from Ammar, that he said, mentioning A'ishah: She is the wife of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this world and the Hereafter."
"1423","1409 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Wa'il, who said: When Ali sent Ammar to Kufah, Ammar addressed, saying: I know she is his wife in this world and the Hereafter."
"1424","And among what Rabi'ah ibn Najidh narrated from Ammar: 1410 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabi'ah ibn Najidh, who said: On the day of Siffin, Ammar said: Today I meet the beloved, Muhammad and his party; I fought with this banner three times with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this is the fourth. And we do not know Rabi'ah ibn Najidh narrated from Ammar except this hadith."
"1425","And among what Hammam ibn al-Harith narrated from Ammar: 1411 - Umar ibn Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, saying: My father Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Bayan, from Wabarah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Musli, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, who said: Ammar said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with none but five slaves, two women, and Abu Bakr. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ammar except through this channel with this chain."
"1426","And among what Salman al-Agharr narrated from Ammar: 1412 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, saying: al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Salman al-Agharr, from his father, from Ammar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of my community is as rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end. And this hadith has been narrated from Ammar, and this chain is better than the other chains narrated from Ammar."
"1427","And among what Ibn al-Hawtakiyyah narrated from Ammar: 1413 - Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of Abu Talhah, from Ibn al-Hawtakiyyah, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not eat of a gift until its giver was trusted, or he would eat thereof, for the sheep gifted to him at Khaybar. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ammar except through this channel with this chain."
"1428","And among what Ibn al-Hanafiyyah narrated from Ammar: 1414 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, saying: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Maysarah, meaning al-Nahdi, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ammar ibn Yasir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon him and said: Remove the harm, Lord of people, and heal, You are the Healer; there is no healing but Your healing, a healing leaving no sickness. And we do not know for this hadith a path other than this path."
"1429","1415 - Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ammar, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and greeted him, and he returned my greeting, meaning by gesture."
"1430","1416 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: I heard Qays ibn Sa'd narrating from Ata, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ammar: that he greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he returned his greeting while praying in the mosque."
"1431","And among what Yazid Abu Khuthaym narrated from Ammar: 1417 - Musa ibn Abdullah Abu Talhah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Khuthaym, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Khuthaym Abu Yazid, from Ammar ibn Yasir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kunya-named Ali as Abu Turab, and it was among his most beloved kunyas to him. And we do not know Khuthaym narrated except this hadith."
"1432","And among what Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated from Ammar: 1418 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Abi Bakr al-Adawi narrated to me, saying: Abdullah ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir narrated to me, from his father, from Miqsam Abu al-Qasim, freedman of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, that Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to him: that Ammar ibn Yasir, when he heard what people discussed of the marriage of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Khadijah, would say, Ammar: I am among the most knowledgeable of people of the marriage of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to her. I was of his brethren, his intimate companion and friend in ignorance. And one day I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we passed by the sister of Khadijah, sitting upon a leather mat of hers; so she called me, and I turned to her, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood. So she said: Has your companion no need of marrying Khadijah? So I informed him, and he said: Yes, by my life. So I returned to her and informed her of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. She said: Come to us in the morning tomorrow. So in the morning we came to them, finding they had slaughtered a cow, dressed the father of Khadijah in a robe, and pitched a dome over him. So I spoke to her brother, and he spoke to her father; and he was informed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his station, asking him to marry her to him; so he married her to him. And they prepared food from the cow, and we ate thereof. And her father slept, then awoke, saying: What is this robe, this dome and this food? His daughter who had spoken to Ammar said to him: This robe Muhammad ibn Abdullah, your son-in-law, clothed you with; and a cow he gifted you, which we slaughtered when he married you to Khadijah. So he denied having married her to him, and went out to al-Hijr, while Banu Hashim went out until they came. So he said: Where is your companion whom you claim I married to Khadijah? And when he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and looked at him, he said: If I married her to him, otherwise I have now married her to him. And this hadith, we do not preserve it from Ammar ibn Yasir except through this channel with this chain."
"1433","And among what Khilas ibn Amr narrated from Ammar: 1419 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, saying: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khilas ibn Amr, from Ammar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Table came down as bread and meat; and they were commanded not to betray, nor store, nor hide for tomorrow; so they betrayed, stored and hid for tomorrow; so it was raised. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ammar, raised, except through this channel."
"1434","1420 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, who said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, that Ammar prayed a prayer of two units; so Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith said to him: You lightened them. He said: Did you see me diminish aught of its bowing or its limits? He said: No, but you lightened them. He said: I hastened therewith against whispering; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man prays the prescribed prayer, and perhaps he has of his prayer but a tenth, a ninth, an eighth, a seventh, a sixth, a fifth, until he reached the end of the count."
"1435","1421 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, saying: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Abdullah ibn Anamah, from Ammar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. And Ibn Ishaq said therein, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Ammar."
"1436","1422 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, who said: Ammar led us in prayer, lightening it; so a man said to him: You lightened it. He said: Did you see me diminish aught of its bowing or its limits? He said: No, but you lightened it. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man prays the prayer, and perhaps he has of his prayer but a tenth, a ninth, an eighth, a seventh, a sixth, a fifth, until he reached the end of the count."
"1437","And among what Abdullah ibn Salamah narrated from Ammar: 1423 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Muradi, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: The idolaters satirized us, and we complained thereof to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he said: Answer them. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ammar except with this chain."
"1438","And among what Abdullah ibn Ubaydah narrated from Ammar: 1424 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, saying: Bakkar, nephew of Musa ibn Ubaydah, narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Ubaydah, from Ammar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: The most wretched of the first is the hamstringer of the she-camel; and the most wretched of the last is he who strikes you a blow upon this; and he gestured to his head; dyeing this; and he gestured to his beard. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ammar except through this channel."
"1439","Ibn al-Himyari from Ammar: 1425 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: Nu'aym ibn Damdam narrated to us, from Ibn al-Himyari, who said: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has entrusted to my grave an angel granted the hearing of creatures; and none invokes blessings upon me until the Day of Resurrection but he conveys to me his name and his father's name: This is so-and-so son of so-and-so who invoked blessings upon you."
"1440","1426 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, saying: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Nu'aym ibn Damdam narrated to us, from Ibn al-Himyari, who said: I heard Ammar narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned similar to it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ammar except with this chain."
"1441","1427 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu Yazid al-Himyari, that he heard Ammar ibn Yasir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Khadijah has been favored over the women of my community as Maryam was favored over the women of the worlds."
"1442","What Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl narrated from Ammar: 1428 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, saying: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Ammar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to him: The rebellious party shall kill you. And this hadith, Abu al-Tayyah narrated it from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, without saying from Ammar."
"1443","Al-Mukhariq ibn Sulaym from Ammar: 1429 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Uqbah ibn al-Mughirah al-Shaybani narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from his father, from al-Mukhariq ibn Sulaym, who said: I saw Ammar on the day of the Camel, with a horn, greasing it with urine therein; so I said: I love to fight with you. So he said: Fight under the banner of your people; for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved that a man fight under the banner of his people. And this hadith, we do not know any who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ammar; and we do not know for it a chain from Ammar except this chain."
"1444","Abu Rashid from Ammar: 1430 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, saying: al-Ala ibn Salih narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Rashid, from Ammar, that he spoke briefly; so it was said to him: You said a word; would that you add for us? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to shorten the sermons. And we do not know Abu Rashid narrated from Ammar except this hadith."
"1445","Nujayy al-Hadrami from Ammar: 1431 - Abbad ibn Ahmad al-Arzami narrated to us, saying: My uncle Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, saying: Jabir narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from his father Nujayy al-Hadrami, who said: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a clan of Qays to teach them the laws of Islam. He said: And they were a people as wild camels with roving eyes, caring for naught but sheep or camel. So I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Ammar, what did you do? So I related to him the story of the people, informing him of their heedlessness. He said: O Ammar, shall I not inform you of more wondrous than them: a people who knew what those were ignorant of, then grew heedless as their heedlessness. And these words, we do not know any who narrated them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ammar; and they are not narrated from Ammar except with this chain."
"1446","Mikhraq, freedman of Hudhayfah, from Ammar: 1432 - Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Muslim, called Abu Dawud al-A'ma, narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la ibn Amir al-Tha'labi, from Abdullah ibn Sharik al-Amiri, from Muslim ibn Mikhraq, from Mikhraq, freedman of Hudhayfah, who said: I said to Ammar: Have you a drink? He said: I empty it all; my beloved narrated to me that my last drink of this world is a thin draught of milk until I come to him at the Basin."
"1447","Abu Ushshanah from Ammar: 1433 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Dawud al-Harrani, brother of Abd al-Ghaffar, narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Ushshanah, who said: I heard Abu al-Yaqzan Ammar ibn Yasir saying: By Allah, you love the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more intensely than those who saw him, or than most of those who saw him. And this hadith, we do not know for it a chain from Ammar except this chain."
"1448","Musnad of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him; fifteenth part; beginning of the musnad of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud; Ibn Umar from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 1434 - Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Hanash, from Ata, meaning Ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour shall not rise until the hypocrites of every tribe rule it. And this hadith, we do not know any who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abdullah ibn Mas'ud; and we do not know for it a path from Abdullah except this path; and this Hanash is Husayn ibn Qays al-Rahabi by name; and more than one narrated from him, saying: Husayn ibn Qays; and we do not know anyone who said Hanash except al-Taymi."
"1449","1435 - Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Qays, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The feet of a servant shall not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked: Of his youth, wherein he wore it out; of his life, wherein he spent it; of his wealth, whence he earned it and wherein he spent it; and of his knowledge, what he did therein. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud except through this channel; and we have already mentioned Husayn ibn Qays with his pliancy, so we sufficed without repeating it; and we do not know Ibn Umar narrated from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud except these two hadiths."
"1450","Ibn Abbas from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: 1436 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, saying: al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dili, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I found Abu Jahl, may Allah curse him, among the slain of Badr with a breath of life remaining; so I severed his head and brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the head of Abu Jahl. So he said: This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the head of Abu Jahl? He said: And that was the oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Yes. So I placed it before him, and he praised Allah. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Mas'ud, except through this channel, connected."
"1451","1437 - And Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Hajjaj, from Hanash, from Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Mas'ud: that he performed ablution for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn with nabidh, so he performed ablution, and said: ""Pure water."" And this hadith is not established against Ibn Lahi'ah, because Ibn Lahi'ah's books had burned, so he used to read from the books of others, so among his hadiths came objectionable hadiths, and this is among them. And we do not know of Ibn Abbas narrating from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud except these two hadiths."
"1452","Abu Hurayrah from Ibn Mas'ud. 1438 - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi and al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn as-Salt Abu Ya'la at-Tawwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja' al-Makki narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: I used to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in prayer and he would return the greeting to me or to us. Then when we came from Abyssinia we greeted him and he did not return it to us, so we said: we used to greet you and you would return it to us. He said: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, introduces in the night and day whatever He wills. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah from Ibn Mas'ud except from this angle with this chain, and we do not know anyone narrated it except Abu Ya'la from Abdullah ibn Raja' with this chain connected, and it has been narrated from Ibn Sirin, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that he used to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in prayer, similar to this, mursal. And we do not know of Abu Hurayrah narrating from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1453","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from him. 1439 - Muhammad ibn Humayd wrote to me informing me in his letter that Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to him, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A person is with the one he loves."" And we do not know of Abu Sa'id narrating from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud except this hadith, and we do not know for it a path except this path."
"1454","And among what Imran ibn Husayn narrated from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. 1440 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and al-Ala' ibn Ziyad, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud."
"1455","1441 - And Abbas an-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and al-Ala' ibn Ziyad, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: We were talking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night until we stayed up late in talk, then we returned to our homes, and when morning came we went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prophets were shown to me tonight with their followers from their nations. A prophet would pass with three of his people with him, and a prophet with a group of his people with him, and a prophet with some men of his people with him, and a prophet with no one of his people with him, until Musa ibn Imran passed by me with a large company of the Children of Israel. When I saw them they pleased me, so I said: My Lord, who are these? He said: This is your brother Musa ibn Imran and those who followed him of the Children of Israel. I said: My Lord, then where is my nation? It was said: Look to your right, and behold the hills, the hills of Makkah, filled with the faces of men. So I said: My Lord, who are these? I was told: your nation. Then I was told: Are you pleased? So I said: My Lord, I am pleased, my Lord, I am pleased. Then I was told: Look to your left, and behold the horizon filled with the faces of men. I said: My Lord, who are these? It was said: your nation. He said: Then I was told: Are you pleased? He said: I said: My Lord, I am pleased, my Lord, I am pleased. Then I was told: Indeed with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. Then Ukkashah ibn Mihsan, a man of Banu Asad ibn Khuzaymah, rose and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them. He said: ""O Allah, make him among them."" Then another man rose and said: O Prophet of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them, so he said: ""Ukkashah has preceded you in it."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May my father and mother be ransom for you."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May my father and mother be ransom for you; if you are able to be of the seventy, then be. But if you are unable or fall short, then be of the people of the hills. But if you are unable and fall short, then be of the people of the horizon. For I saw there people crowding in great number."" Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed I hope that those who followed me of my nation will be a quarter of the people of Paradise."" He said: So we said takbir. Then he said: ""Indeed I hope they will be a third."" He said: So we said takbir. Then he said: ""Indeed I hope you will be half."" So we said takbir. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {A group of the first and a group of the last}. So the Muslims discussed: Who are these? We do not see them except those born in Islam who continued acting upon it until they died upon it. He said: Then their talk reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""Not so, but they are those who do not seek ruqyah, nor cauterize, nor take omens, and upon their Lord they rely."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain."
"1456","Anas ibn Malik from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. 1442 - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed the last one to enter Paradise is a man who walks once and stumbles once, and falls into the Fire once. Then when he passes beyond it he turns to it and says: Blessed is He who saved me from you; Allah has given me something He has not given anyone of the first and the last. He said: Then Allah raises for him a tree, or a tree is raised for him, so he says: My Lord, bring me near to this tree so I may shade in its shade and drink from its water. So He says: O son of Adam, perhaps if I give it to you, you will ask Me for other than it. He said: So he says: No, my Lord. He said: So He says, and he promises Him not to ask Him for other than it. He said: And his Lord excuses him, because he sees that which he has no patience over, so He brings him near to it, and he shades in its shade and drinks from its water. Then a tree better than the first is raised for him, so he says: Bring me near to this tree so I may drink from its water and shade in its shade; I will not ask You for other than it. So He says: O son of Adam, did you not promise me not to ask Me for other than it? And his Lord excuses him because he sees that which he has no patience over, so He says: Perhaps if I bring you near to it you will ask Me for other than it, so he says: No, this one, this one. So He brings him near to it, and he shades in its shade and drinks from its water. Then a tree at the gate of Paradise, better than the first two, is raised for him, so he says: My Lord, bring me near to this tree so I may shade in its shade and drink from its water; I will not ask You for other than it. So He says: O son of Adam, did you not promise me not to ask Me for other than it? So he says: Yes, this one, I will not ask You for other than it. And his Lord excuses him because he sees that which he has no patience over. So He brings him near to it, then he hears the voices of the people of Paradise, so he says: My Lord, admit me into it. So He says: O son of Adam, what will make you stop asking? Will it please you if I give you the world and its like with it? So he says: My Lord, are You mocking me while You are the Lord of the worlds? Then Ibn Mas'ud laughed and said: Why do you not ask me why I laughed? They said: Why did you laugh? He said: This is how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, and they said: Why do you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Because of the laughter of the Lord of the worlds when he said: Are You mocking me while You are the Lord of the worlds? So He says: I am not mocking you, but I am Able over whatever I will. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas from Ibn Mas'ud except with this chain."
"1457","Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr from Ibn Mas'ud. 1443 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that he reported to him that he said: There were only four years between their acceptance of Islam and the revelation of this verse by which Allah reproached them: {And let them not be like those who were given the Book before, so the term became long for them}. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud except with this chain, and we do not know of Ibn az-Zubayr narrating from Ibn Mas'ud except this hadith."
"1458","Wabisah ibn Ma'bad al-Asadi from him. 1444 - Salamah ibn Shabib and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from Amr ibn Wabisah al-Asadi, from his father, he said: I was in my house in Kufah when I heard at the door of the house: Peace be upon you, may I enter? So I said: And upon you peace, enter. When he entered, behold, it was Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. So I said: O Abu Abdir-Rahman, what a time for a visit this is? And that was around midday. He said: The day grew long for me so I remembered someone to talk to, so he began narrating to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I would narrate to him. Then he began narrating to me and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be a tribulation; the sleeper in it is better than the one lying down, and the one lying down in it is better than the walker, and the walker in it is better than the rider, and the rider in it is better than the runner; all its slain are in the Fire. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and when is that time? He said: That is the days of al-harj. He said: I said: And what are the days of al-harj? He said: When a man does not feel safe with his companion. I said: Then what do you command me if I reach that time? He said: Enter your house. I said: Then if someone enters upon me in my house? He said: Then enter your mosque, and place your hand like this, and he clasped his right hand over the wrist, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Until you are killed upon that. And we do not know of Wabisah ibn Ma'bad narrating from Ibn Mas'ud except this hadith with this chain."
"1459","Amr ibn Hurayth from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. 1445 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from al-Qasim ibn Abdir-Rahman: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abdullah ibn Mas'ud to recite Surah an-Nisa' to him, so he recited. Al-Mas'udi said: Then Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Hurayth narrated to me from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: When I reached {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you over these as a witness}, the one beside me nudged me, and behold the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had filled with tears, so I stopped reciting. And we do not know of Amr ibn Hurayth narrating from Ibn Mas'ud except this hadith."
"1460","Shaddad ibn al-Hadi from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. 1446 - Abu Kurayb, Ahmad ibn Uthman, and Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, they said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Kaysan, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed the closest of you to me on the Day of Resurrection are those who sent most blessings upon me in the world."" And this hadith, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated it thus, and Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah narrated it from Musa ibn Ya'qub, from Abdullah ibn Kaysan, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Mas'ud, and Muhammad ibn Khalid did not say, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from his father. And we do not know of Shaddad ibn al-Had narrating from Ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except this hadith."
"1461","Abu at-Tufayl from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. 1447 - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Rabi'ah ibn Kulthum narrated to us, from his father, from Abu at-Tufayl, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, marfu': The wretched is he who is wretched in his mother's womb. When the sperm-drop falls into the womb, an angel descends to it. Then when Allah decrees the creation of what is in her belly, the angel says: My Lord, male or female? So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, decrees, and the angel writes. Then he says: My Lord, what is his deed? So Allah decrees to the angel, and the angel writes. Then he says: My Lord, wretched or happy? So Allah decrees to the angel, and the angel writes. And this hadith has been narrated by a group from Abu at-Tufayl from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud mawquf, and from Hudhayfah ibn Asid marfu', and Rabi'ah ibn Kulthum ibn Jabr related it musnad from his father, from Abu at-Tufayl, from Ibn Mas'ud. And we do not know of Abu at-Tufayl relating musnad from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1462","Buraydah from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. 1448 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Salih ibn Hayyan, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father: that he used to mention the tashahhud from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know of Buraydah narrating from Abdullah except this hadith, and we do not know for it a path from Buraydah except this path, and we heard it only from Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ahwazi."
"1463","Abu Shurayh from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. 1449 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl, from Sufyan ibn Abi al-Awja', from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of Uthman, so he led the people in prayer two rak'ahs with two prostrations in each rak'ah. Then Uthman left and entered his house, and Ibn Mas'ud sat beside the chamber of A'ishah, so we sat with him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us at the eclipse of the sun and the moon to pray, and said: ""When you see it befall"" - I think he said - ""then hasten to prayer, for if it is what you fear, and if not, you have attained good or earned it."" And we do not know of Abu Shurayh narrating from Abdullah except this hadith, and it has no path from Abdullah except this path."
"1464","Tariq ibn Shihab from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1450 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah has not sent down a disease except He sent down for it a cure, so upon you is cow's milk, for it grazes from every tree."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Sufyan with this chain except Muhammad ibn Yusuf."
"1465","1451 - And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it, from the hadith of ath-Thawri from Qays ibn Muslim."
"1466","1452 - And as-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Zayd Sa'id ibn ar-Rabi' narrated to us from Shu'bah. 1453 - And Salamah narrated it to us, he said: Al-Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Shu'bah, both of them mentioned it from Shu'bah, from ar-Rabi' ibn ar-Rukayn, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has not sent down a disease except He sent down for it a cure."" And we do not know of ar-Rabi' ibn ar-Rukayn narrating from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq, from Abdullah except this hadith, and this hadith was narrated from Shu'bah by Abu Zayd, al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, and al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr."
"1467","1454 - And Zayd ibn Akhzam at-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: Utbah ibn Yaqzan narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""No good deed of a doer of good, Muslim or disbeliever, goes unrewarded."" We said: O Messenger of Allah, the reward of the believer we know, so what is the reward of the disbeliever? He said: ""When he gives charity or joins kinship or does a good deed, Allah rewards him, and his reward is wealth and children in this world, and a punishment less than the punishment,"" meaning in the Hereafter, and he recited {Admit the people of Pharaoh into the severest punishment}. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, and we do not know for it a chain from Abdullah except this chain."
"1468","1455 - And al-Hasan ibn Arafah and Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, they said: Abu Yahya at-Taymi narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: I witnessed from al-Miqdad a stand, that I be its owner is more beloved to me than the earth filled with anything. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he became angry his cheeks would redden, so he came while he was in that state and said: O Messenger of Allah, we will not say to you as the Children of Israel said to Musa: (Go, you and your Lord, and fight; indeed we are sitting here), but by the One who sent you with the truth, we will surely be before you, behind you, to your right, and to your left."
"1469","1456 - And Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated it to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq, from Abdullah, that he said: I witnessed from al-Miqdad, then he mentioned similar to this speech. And we do not know of Mukhariq relating musnad from Tariq from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1470","1457 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, from Sayyar, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be in my nation collapse, metamorphosis, and pelting."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"1471","1458 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bashir narrated to us, from Sayyar, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is afflicted with poverty and brings it to people, they will not satisfy his poverty, but if he brings it to Allah, Allah is soon to satisfy his poverty."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"1472","1459 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bashir Abu Isma'il narrated to us, from Sayyar, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Among the signs of the nearness of the Hour is greeting by acquaintance, and that a man passes by the mosque and does not pray in it."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Tariq from Abdullah except from this angle."
"1473","And among what Abu Umamah al-Bahili, whose name is Sudayy ibn Ajlan, narrated from Abdullah. 1460 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Zahr narrated to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The deeds of the children of Adam are presented every Monday and every Thursday; so the merciful ones are shown mercy, and the seekers of forgiveness are forgiven, and the people of malice are left with their rancor."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"1474","1461 - And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There will surely come upon you a time when you will envy a man for lightness of burden as you envy him today for abundance of wealth and children, until one of you passes by the grave of his brother and rolls as a beast rolls, and says: Would that I were in your place. It is not out of loving longing for Allah nor a righteous deed he put forth, except because of the tribulation that befell him."""
"1475","And among what Zaynab, the wife of Abdullah, narrated from Abdullah. 1462 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl and Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Salamah, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Zaynab, the wife of Abdullah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: I do not know it except he raised it - thus said al-Fadl, and Ahmad ibn Ishaq raised it - he said: ""A woman is not married over her paternal aunt, nor over her maternal aunt, and a woman should not ask for the divorce of her sister to empty what is in her bowl."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"1476","And among what Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1463 - Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Hunayn, and he wanted to relieve himself, and when he wanted that he would go far so no one would see him. He said: ""Look, do you see anything?"" So I looked and saw a single lote-tree, so I informed him. Then he said: ""Look, do you see anything?"" So I looked at another lote-tree far from its companion, so I informed him. Then he said to me: Tell them both that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to come together. So I told them that, and they came together. Then he came to them and screened himself with them. Then he stood, and when he had relieved himself, each one went back to its place. Then the people suffered severe thirst in that expedition, so he said to Abdullah: ""Seek for me,"" meaning water. So I brought him leftover water I found in a waterskin. So he took it and poured it into a vessel, then placed his hand in it and mentioned the name, and water began to flow from between his fingers. So the people drank and performed ablution as much as they wished. So Abdullah said: I knew it was a blessing, so I began drinking from it abundantly, seeking its blessing. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the direction of Madinah, and a camel whose eyes had shed tears met him. So he said: ""To whom does this camel belong?"" They said: To Banu so-and-so. He said: ""For it has sought refuge with me."" He said: They had intended to slaughter it, and they had worked it until it grew old and worn out. He said: ""Do not slaughter it, and be kind to it, for evil is what you have rewarded it."" And we do not know of Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrating from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1477","Al-Mughirah from Ibrahim. 1464 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, he said: That was mentioned by Shibak to Ibrahim, so he said: We asked Alqamah about that, so he narrated to us from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba and its giver. So I said: And its writer and its two witnesses? And he said: We only narrate what we heard."
"1478","1465 - And Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, he said: an-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam and al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr five rak'ahs, so it was said to him: Has something been added to the prayer? So he said: ""And what is that?"" He said: You prayed five. So he folded his leg and prostrated two prostrations."
"1479","1466 - And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"1480","The first hadith of Alqamah from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1467 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abdir-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah said: May Allah curse the tattooing women and those seeking tattooing, the plucking women, and those who make gaps for beauty, who change the creation of Allah. He said: That reached a woman of Banu Asad called Umm Ya'qub, so she came to him and said: What hadith has reached me from you? So she mentioned it to him, so he said: Why should I not curse whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed, and it is in the Book of Allah."
"1481","1468 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna ibn Ubayd narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the tattooing women and those seeking tattooing."
"1482","1469 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir Abu Attab narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah said: May Allah curse the tattooing women and those seeking tattooing, the plucking women, and those who make gaps for beauty, who change the creation of Allah. Then that reached a woman of Banu Asad called Umm Ya'qub who used to recite the Qur'an, so she came to him and said: What hadith has reached me from you? That you cursed the tattooing women and those seeking tattooing, the plucking women, and those who make gaps for beauty, who change the creation of Allah. So Abdullah said: And why should I not curse whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed, and it is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. So the woman said: I have recited what is between the two covers of the mushaf and I did not find that in it. So he said: {And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it}. So the woman said: The first thing of this is upon your wife. He said: Then go and look. So the woman entered and saw nothing. Then she came to him and said: I saw nothing. So he said: Had that been so - and he mentioned a word - Abu Bakr said: meaning, she would not have stayed with me. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah."
"1483","1470 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1484","1471 - And Ja'far ibn Akhi Waki' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you doubts in prayer, let him seek the correct, then prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness."" And we do not know of Mis'ar narrating from Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1485","1472 - Bishr ibn Hilal as-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn az-Zibriqan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the story of forgetfulness, similar in these wordings."
"1486","1473 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abdil-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer and added in it or decreased. Then when he gave salam, it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, has something new happened in the prayer? He said: ""No, and what is that?"" They said: You prayed such and such. So he folded his leg, faced the qiblah, prostrated two prostrations, then gave salam. Then when he gave salam he turned to us with his face and said: ""Indeed, had something new happened in the prayer I would have informed you of it, but I am only a human; I forget as you forget. So when I forget, remind me. And when one of you doubts in prayer, let him seek the correct, complete upon it, then give salam, then prostrate two prostrations."""
"1487","1474 - And al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, he said: al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us, and when he gave salam he turned to us with his face, and he mentioned similar to it."
"1488","1475 - And Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to the hadith of Jarir."
"1489","1476 - Ibrahim ibn Bistam and Ahmad ibn Abdullah as-Sadusi narrated to us, they said: Mu'ammal narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O company of youths, whoever among you has means, let him marry; otherwise upon him is fasting, for it is a restraint."" And this hadith, we do not preserve it from the hadith of Mansur from Ibrahim with this chain except from the hadith of Mu'ammal from Sufyan, and it is only known from the hadith of Sufyan from al-A'mash; so Mu'ammal combined, from Sufyan, from Mansur and al-A'mash."
"1490","1477 - And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave, and a snake came out, so we rushed toward it, but it outran us and entered a hole. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was protected from your evil as you were protected from its evil. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except Isra'il."
"1491","1478 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We used to count the signs as blessing, and you count them as fright. We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and water became scarce, so he said: ""Seek."" So I said: Is there any water? Then a vessel with a little water was brought, so he put his hand into the vessel and said: Come to the blessed purification, and blessing is from Allah. I saw water springing from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we were satisfied, and we used to hear the glorification of food while it was being eaten. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Mansur with this chain except Isra'il."
"1492","1479 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, that they both entered upon Abdullah, so he said: Have these prayed? So they said: Yes. So he stood between them, placing one of them to his right and the other to his left. Then we bowed and placed our hands upon our knees, so he struck our hands, then clasped, then placed them between his thighs. Then when he prayed he said: This is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Mansur with this chain except Isra'il."
"1493","1480 - And Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Jabalah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah as-Sukkari narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr and Umar, in Mina, two rak'ahs. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Mansur from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah except Abu Hamzah."
"1494","1481 - And Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he ascended the minbar, would face us with his face. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Mansur with this chain except Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah, and he is lenient in hadith, and none but he narrated it, so we mentioned it for that reason."
"1495","1482 - And al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Awn Abu Awn narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened two years' charity from al-Abbas. And this hadith, the memorizers only narrate it from Mansur, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, mursal; and this Muhammad ibn Dhakwan is lenient in hadith; he narrated many hadiths not corroborated upon."
"1496","1483 - And Abdullah ibn as-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among people, then al-Hasan and al-Husayn passed by him, so he said: Bring my two sons to me so I may seek refuge for them with what Ibrahim sought refuge for his two sons Isma'il and Ishaq: I seek refuge for you both with the perfect words of Allah from every devil and vermin, and from every evil eye. And this hadith, Muhammad ibn Dhakwan erred in it; he narrated it from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, while the correct is what Mansur narrated, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas."
"1497","Al-Hakam from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. 1484 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he prayed Zuhr five rak'ahs. So it was said: Has something been added to the prayer? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""And what is that?"" They said: You prayed five. So he prostrated two prostrations after he gave salam."
"1498","1485 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: al-Hakam narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr five rak'ahs. So it was said to him: Has something been added to the prayer? He said: ""And what is that?"" They said: You prayed five. So he folded his leg and prostrated two prostrations."
"1499","1486 - And Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr an-Nahshali narrated to us, from al-Haytham as-Sayrafi, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to the hadith of Yahya ibn Sa'id. And the hadith of Shu'bah from al-Hakam has been narrated by more than one from Shu'bah, and the hadith of Haytham as-Sayrafi from al-Hakam, we do not know anyone narrated it from him except Abu Bakr an-Nahshali."
"1500","1487 - And Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Indeed in prayer there is occupation."" And this hadith has been narrated by other than Abu Khalid, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah."
"1501","1488 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1502","1489 - And Hatim ibn Bakr adh-Dharra' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Huna'i narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""O company of youths, whoever among you has means, let him marry; otherwise upon him is fasting, for it is a restraint for him."" And this hadith, we heard it only from Hatim ibn Bakr, from Muhammad ibn Abbad, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam with this chain, and it was not corroborated; and Hatim was of sound mind and good understanding, so this hadith was borne from him, even though none but he corroborated him upon it; and this hadith is only preserved from Shu'bah from al-A'mash."
"1503","1490 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, they said: Ubayd ibn as-Sabbah al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Kamil ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, from al-Hakam, meaning Ibn Utaybah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions were with him, when a naked woman came. So a man of the people stood to her, threw a garment over her and embraced her. So the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed. So some of his companions said: I think she is his wife. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I think her other than jealous, and that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has written jealousy upon women and jihad upon men; so whoever of them is patient, she will have the reward of a martyr. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain. And Ubayd ibn as-Sabbah is unobjectionable, and Kamil ibn al-Ala' is well-known of the people of Kufah; a group of scholars narrated from him and bore his hadith, though none shared with him in this hadith."
"1504","1491 - And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dahir ar-Razi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned youths of Banu Hashim and his eyes filled with tears, and he mentioned the black banners, and said: Whoever reaches them, let him come to them, even crawling upon snow. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Hakam except Ibn Abi Layla, and we do not know it narrated except from the hadith of Dahar ibn Yahya from Ibn Abi Layla. And this Dahar is a man of the people of opinion, sound in hadith, and it is only known from the hadith of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Ibrahim."
"1505","1492 - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya and Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, they said: Musaddad narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: A man of the polytheists said to Abdullah: I think your companion has taught you everything, even teaching you how to relieve yourselves? He said: If you are mocking, he has taught us not to face the qiblah with our private parts, and I think he said: nor to cleanse with our right hands, nor to cleanse with dung, nor to cleanse with bone, nor to cleanse with less than three stones. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Hakam except Sufyan ibn Husayn, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Husayn ibn Numayr except Musaddad. And this hadith is only known from the hadith of al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abdir-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Salman; and Mansur narrated it from Ibrahim, from Abdir-Rahman ibn Yazid, from some companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1506","Al-A'mash from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1493 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: When {Those who believed and did not mix their faith with wrong} was revealed, that was hard upon the people, and they said: Which of us does not wrong himself? He said: It is not what you mean. Have you not heard what the righteous servant said: {O my son, do not associate with Allah; indeed association is a great wrong}."
"1507","1494 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: When this verse was revealed: {Those who believed and did not mix their faith with wrong}, that was hard upon the people, and they said: Which of us does not wrong himself? He said: It is not what you mean. Have you not heard what the righteous servant said: {O my son, do not associate with Allah; indeed association is a great wrong}. Ibn Idris said: I had heard it from my father, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from al-A'mash, then I met al-A'mash and he narrated it to me."
"1508","1495 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah; and Shu'bah narrated it from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah."
"1509","1496 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: A man of the People of the Book came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim, has it reached you that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, carries the creatures upon a finger, the heavens upon a finger, the earths upon a finger, the trees upon a finger, and the soil upon a finger? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared, and recited {And they did not esteem Allah His true esteem}."
"1510","1497 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Musawir al-Fadl ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. Thus al-A'mash narrated it from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah; and ath-Thawri narrated it from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah."
"1511","1498 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur and Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah. And Yahya said, and Fudayl ibn Iyad added, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed in wonder and affirmation."
"1512","1499 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I was in Hims, and the people said to me: Recite to us. So I recited Surah Yusuf to them. Then a man of the people said: By Allah, it was not revealed thus. So I said: Woe to you; by Allah, I recited it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said to me: ""You did well."" Then while I was speaking to him I noticed the smell of wine from him. So I said: You drink wine and deny the Book? I will not leave until I flog you. So he flogged him the hadd."
"1513","1500 - And Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, and he mentioned similar to it, and said: I recited it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: You did well. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Abdullah ibn Mas'ud."
"1514","1501 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abdil-Hamid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I was on a Friday night in the mosque when a man of the Ansar came and said: If a man finds with his wife a man and speaks, you flog him; or if he kills, you kill him; and if he is silent, he is silent in anger. By Allah, I will surely ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then on the morrow he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, saying: If a man finds with his wife a man and speaks, you flog him; and if he kills, you kill him; and if he is silent, he is silent in anger. O Allah, open. So he began supplicating, and the verse of li'an was revealed: {And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses but themselves}, the verse. He said: So that man among the people was tried with it. He said: So he came with his wife to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they invoked mutual curses. So the man bore witness four testimonies by Allah that he is of the truthful, then cursed the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he is of the liars. He said: Then she went to curse, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If she brings him black, curly-haired, then he is of such. So she brought him black, curly-haired."
"1515","1502 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"1516","1503 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I was passing with Abdullah, and Uthman ibn Affan met him and spoke to him. So Uthman said to him: O Abu Abdir-Rahman, will you not marry, or shall I not marry you to a slave girl who will remind you of what has passed of your time? So Abdullah said: Since you said that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: O company of youths, whoever is able, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze; and whoever is not able, upon him is fasting, for it is a restraint for him."
"1517","1504 - And Ibrahim ibn Bistam and Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, they said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""O company of youths, whoever among you has means, let him marry; and whoever does not, upon him is fasting, for it is a restraint for him."""
"1518","1505 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after speech. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-A'mash with this chain."
"1519","1506 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Khabbab ibn al-Aratt entered while we were around Abdullah, so he said to Abdullah: Do all of these recite as you recite? He said: If you wish, I will command one of them to recite to you. He said: So he said to Alqamah: Recite. He said: So Yazid ibn Murrah said: He recites, though he is not the best reciter among us. So Abdullah said: If you wish, I will inform you of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about your people and his people. He said: So I recited to him fifty verses of Surah Maryam, so he said: I do not recite anything except he recites it or recites with it. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-A'mash, so we sufficed with Jarir."
"1520","1507 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We used to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in prayer, and he would return it to us while in prayer. Then when we returned from the Negus, we greeted him and he did not return it to us. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to greet you and you would return it to us. So he said: Indeed in prayer there is occupation. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-A'mash with this chain."
"1521","1508 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"1522","1509 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to the hadith of Ibn Fudayl from al-A'mash."
"1523","1510 - And Ahmad ibn Malik al-Qushayri narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash, Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, and al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me to recite Surah an-Nisa' to him while he was upon the minbar, so I recited until I reached: {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you over these as a witness}. He said: Then his eyes filled with tears, and he said: Whoever is pleased to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd. And this hadith, al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad and Abu al-Ahwas narrated it from al-A'mash with this chain, and others than them narrated it from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Ubaydah, 1511 - from Abdullah. And Ahmad ibn Malik narrated to us with the hadith of Abu al-Ahwas, from al-Hasan ibn ar-Rabi', he said: Abu al-Ahwas Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us."
"1524","1512 - Abdul-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abdul-Aziz ibn Muslim informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None shall enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard grain of pride, and none shall enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a mustard grain of faith."" And this hadith, Abdul-Aziz ibn Muslim and Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated it from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah."
"1525","1513 - Muhammad ibn Abdir-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: When the prohibition of wine was revealed, the Jews said: Were not your brothers who died used to drink it? So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: {There is no blame upon those who believed and did righteous deeds for what they tasted}. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It was said to me: you are of them."""
"1526","1514 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abdil-Karim narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: When this verse was revealed: {There is no blame upon those who believed and did righteous deeds for what they tasted}, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was said to me, you are of them."
"1527","1515 - And Isa ibn Abdullah narrated it to us, he said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, from Qays, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"1528","1516 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Qabisah, meaning Ibn Uqbah, narrated to us, from ath-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Qasa was shaken in the time of Abdullah, so Abdullah said: We used to see the signs with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as blessings, and you see them as fright. And this hadith, Abdur-Razzaq, Qabisah, and others than them narrated it from ath-Thawri with this chain; and Ammar ibn Ruzayq also narrated it from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah."
"1529","1517 - Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: Sa'd used to fight with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr with the fighting of the horseman and the foot soldier."
"1530","1518 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, similar to it, and he did not say from Alqamah."
"1531","1519 - Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham narrated to us, he said: an-Nadr ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was feverish, or he said: suffering fever, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, how severe is your fever? He said: I suffer fever as two men of you suffer. This is his wording or its meaning. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from al-A'mash with this chain except an-Nadr ibn Isma'il."
"1532","1520 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn as-Salt narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he: used to sleep while prostrating, then stand and continue in his prayer. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah except Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, and it was not corroborated; and Mansur is unobjectionable, a shaykh of the people of Kufah."
"1533","1521 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and {By those sent forth in succession} was revealed to him, so I received it from his mouth fresh. And a snake came out against us, so we rushed toward it, but it entered a hole. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was protected from your evil as you were protected from its evil. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-A'mash except Isra'il."
"1534","1522 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The tattooing women, those who make gaps, and the plucking women who change the creation of Allah were cursed. So a woman said to him some speech he mentioned, so Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-A'mash with this chain except Jarir ibn Hazim."
"1535","1523 - Al-Hasan ibn as-Sabbah ibn al-Bazzar and Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The believer is not a stabber, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor foul."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-A'mash except Isra'il, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Isra'il except Muhammad ibn Sabiq."
"1536","1524 - Yahya ibn Yazid, imam of the mosque of al-Ahwaz, wrote to me informing me in his letter that Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn az-Zibriqan narrated to him, he said: Marwan ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The closest a servant is to Allah is while prostrating."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Marwan ibn Salim from al-A'mash, and it was not corroborated; and this Marwan ibn Salim is lenient in hadith, and more than one narrated from him."
"1537","1525 - Ali ibn Muslim at-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Abdil-Majid ibn Abdil-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I went out with Abdullah on Friday. He said: So he entered the mosque and behold three had preceded, so he said: Fourth of four, and what is fourth of four? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: They sit according to their early going to Friday, the first, then the second, then the third, then the fourth. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except Marwan ibn Salim, and our mention of his leniency has preceded."
"1538","1526 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take the Qur'an from four: from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and Salim the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah."" And this hadith, we heard it only from Ibrahim ibn Sa'id, from Ibrahim ibn Mahdi, from Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib."
"1539","1527 - Isma'il ibn Hafs al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked li'an with pregnancy. And this hadith, Abdah abridged it, and Jarir and Abu Awanah narrated it and did not mention this wording."
"1540","1528 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us istikhara: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, and I seek ability from You by Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty and mercy, for they are in Your hand; none owns them but You. For You know and I do not know, and You are able and I am not able, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this matter, for the matter You want, is good for me in my religion and my world - I think he said: and the outcome of my affair - then grant it and ease it; and if other than that is good, then grant me good - I think he said: wherever it is. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from the hadith of al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except Salih ibn Musa, and we heard it only from Ibrahim ibn Sa'id; and Salih is not strong."
"1541","1529 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among date-palms leaning - I think he said: upon a palm stalk - when a Jew confronted him and asked him about the spirit. So he began nodding with his head, and I thought revelation was coming to him. So he said: {And they ask you about the spirit; say: The spirit is of the affair of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge but little}. And this hadith, Waki' and Ali ibn Mushir narrated it from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah; and Ibn Idris differed from them from al-A'mash."
"1542","1530 - Abdullah ibn as-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Mutayyib narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The death of the believer is with sweat on the brow."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone related it musnad from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Qasim ibn Mutayyib."
"1543","1531 - Muhammad ibn Abdil-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: Everything revealed: O people, is in Makkah; and everything revealed: O you who believed, is in Madinah. And this hadith, others than Qays narrate it mursal, and we do not know anyone related it musnad except Qays."
"1544","1532 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he was asked about the major sins, so he said: What is between the beginning of Surah an-Nisa' to the top of thirty."
"1545","What Amr ibn Murrah narrated from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1533 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lay upon a mat, and it marked his side. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, if you commanded us we would take for you a bedding to protect you from the mat? So he said: What have I to do with the world, and what am I and the world? The likeness of me and the world is but as a rider who shaded under a tree, then departed and left it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Amr ibn Murrah except al-Mas'udi, and Amr ibn Murrah did not narrate from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1546","Uthman ibn Umayr from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1534 - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya and Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu an-Nu'man Muhammad ibn al-Fadl as-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The two sons of Mulaykah al-Ju'fiyyayn came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Our mother used to honor the husband and show affection to the child - and they mentioned affection - except that she had buried alive in Jahiliyyah. So he said: Your mother is in the Fire. So they turned away, evil recognized in their faces. So he ordered them and they were returned, joy seen in their faces. So he said: My mother is with your mother. He said: Then a man of the hypocrites said: What does this avail him regarding his father or his parents at all, while we tread upon his heels? So a man of the Ansar said: I never saw anyone more - I think he said: questioning - O Messenger of Allah, has your Lord promised you regarding her or them? So he thought it was of something he had heard. So he said: I have not asked my Lord, nor has He given me hope; and I shall surely stand the Praised Station on the Day of Resurrection. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is the Praised Station? He said: That is when you are brought naked - I think he said: barefoot - for the first to be clothed is Ibrahim the Friend of Allah. So He says: Clothe him, so he is clothed with two garments and wears them. Then he stands facing the Throne. Then I am brought my clothing and I wear it, so I stand at His right, a station none but I stands, envied therein by the first and the last. He said: And a river is opened from al-Kawthar to the Hawd. So the hypocrite said: Rarely did water ever flow except upon pebbles or gravel. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, upon pebbles or gravel? He said: Its pebbles are musk, and its gravel is corundum - meaning pearls. So the hypocrite said: I never heard like today; for water never flowed upon pebbles or gravel except it had vegetation. So the Ansari said: Does it have vegetation? So he said: ""Yes, rods of gold."" So the hypocrite said: I never heard like today; for rarely does a twig grow except it leaves and has fruit. So the Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah, does it have fruit? He said: ""Yes, colors of jewels, and its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. Whoever drinks a drink of it will never thirst after, and whoever is deprived of it will never be quenched after."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording from the hadith of Alqamah from Abdullah except from this angle. And as-Saq ibn Hazn narrated it from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah; and I think as-Saq erred in this chain."
"1547","Ibn Shubrumah from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1535 - Ali ibn Dawud and Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shubrumah, and he is Abdullah ibn Shubrumah, narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: Whoever wishes, I will swear to him or invoke mutual curse that {And for pregnant women their term is that they deliver their burden} was revealed after the verse of the deceased, so when the widow delivers her burden she has become lawful; and he recited {And those of you who die and leave wives} to the end of the verse. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Ibn Shubrumah except Muhammad ibn Ja'far, and we do not know of Ibn Shubrumah narrating from Ibrahim with this chain except this hadith."
"1548","Ubaydah ibn Mu'attib from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1536 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dawud informed us, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left."
"1549","1537 - And al-Harith ibn al-Khidr narrated it to us, he said: Uthman ibn Farqad narrated to us, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. And we do not know of Ubaydah narrating from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1550","Simak ibn Harb from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1538 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, or al-Aswad, from Abdullah."
"1551","1539 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from Simak, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I met a woman on one of the roads of Madinah, and I obtained from her everything short of intercourse. He said: Then {And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds}, the verse, was revealed. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for him specifically or for people generally? He said: Rather for people generally. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Simak, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad; and some of them doubted, saying from Alqamah or al-Aswad, from Abdullah."
"1552","1540 - And Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from Simak, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, marfu', he said: He said: Which charity is best? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That a man lends his brother dirhams, or the back of a mount. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Simak, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah except from the hadith of Hafs ibn Jumay' from Simak, and we heard it only from Umar ibn Yahya."
"1553","1541 - Tulayq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ata, from Simak, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mina, and the moon split. And this hadith, Simak narrated it thus, and al-A'mash narrated it from Ibrahim, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah."
"1554","Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1542 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The mother of Abdullah and the wife of Abdullah went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each concealing her affair from her companion. So they came to the chamber and said to Bilal: Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say: Two women; one has surplus wealth, and in her care are her brother's orphaned sons; and the other said: I have surplus wealth, and I have a husband light of means. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Two shares, two shares - meaning by their charity upon those they mentioned. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except Ibrahim ibn Muhajir."
"1555","1543 - Ahmad ibn Malik al-Qushayri narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir and others, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me to recite Surah an-Nisa', so I recited until I reached: {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you over these as a witness}. Then his eyes filled with tears, and he said: Whoever is pleased to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except al-Mufaddal; and Shu'bah narrated it from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah mursal, without placing Alqamah between them."
"1556","Abu Ma'shar Ziyad ibn Kulayb from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1544 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let those of you with understanding and intellect be nearest to me, then those next to them""; and he forbade the clamors of the markets. And this hadith with this wording, I do not know anyone narrated it from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except Abu Ma'shar, nor from Abu Ma'shar except Khalid al-Hadhdha'."
"1557","1545 - Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I was not with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn, and I wished I had been with him. And this hadith, we do not preserve it from the hadith of Khalid al-Hadhdha' except from the hadith of Khalid ibn Abdullah from him."
"1558","1546 - Ishaq ibn Ziyad al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, marfu', he said: The death of the believer is with sweat on the brow."
"1559","1547 - And Muhammad ibn Abdil-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Yunus, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The death of the believer is with sweat on the brow. And this hadith, Husam ibn Misakk related it musnad from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1560","1548 - Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated it to us, he said: Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Husam ibn Misakk narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1561","Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1549 - Muhammad ibn Abdir-Rahim Sahib as-Sabiri and Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim at-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Abdus-Salam, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast while traveling and break fast. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah except from this angle with this chain, and we do not know anyone narrated it from this Abdus-Salam except Ibn Abi Arubah."
"1562","1550 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: Utbah ibn Yaqzan narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from his maternal uncles, meaning Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: A group of Jews came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, if you are a prophet as you mention, inform us whence resemblance comes: a man resembles his paternal uncles once, and his maternal uncles once. So he said: The water of the man is white and thick, and the water of the woman is yellow and thin; so whichever of them overcomes, the resemblance prevails."
"1563","1551 - And Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: Utbah ibn Yaqzan narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from his maternal uncles, meaning Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's belly forty days, then he is a clot like that - I think he said: then he is a lump like that - then Allah sends to him the angel, and he is commanded with four words. So it is said: Write for him his term, his deed, his provision, and wretched or happy. For one of you does the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is between him and it but a cubit, then the writing overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of the Fire and enters it. And a man does the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is between him and it but a cubit, then the writing overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of Paradise - I think he said: and enters it."" And these two hadiths, we do not know them narrated from the hadith of Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah except from this angle, and we heard them only from Ahmad ibn Ishaq, from Amir ibn Mudrik."
"1564","1552 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Ali al-Hanafi Ubaydullah ibn Abdil-Majid narrated to us, he said: Ka'b ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub and pray with us while his head dripped, then fast that day. And this hadith, we heard it only from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from al-Hanafi."
"1565","1553 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Zarbi narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""A beautiful voice is an adornment of the Qur'an."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except Sa'id ibn Zarbi; and this Sa'id ibn Zarbi is not strong."
"1566","1554 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, he said: Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi Abdir-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon are two signs of the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life. So when you see that, hasten to prayer, or pray."
"1567","1555 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakim ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Ufayr ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach them the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. And this hadith, Shu'bah and others narrated it from Hammad, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah; and I think Ufayr ibn Ma'dan erred in it when he made it from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah."
"1568","Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1556 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abdil-Hamid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), youths of Banu Hashim passed, and his eyes filled with tears. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, we continually see in your face something we dislike. He said: We are a household for whom Allah has chosen the Hereafter over the world; and my household will meet after me preference and expulsion in the lands, until Allah raises people from here - and he gestured with his hand toward the east - so they ask for the right and are not given it, then they ask for the right and are not given it, three times, then they fight and prevail, until they raise it to a man who fills it with justice as it was filled with injustice. So whoever of you reaches that, let him come to them, even crawling upon snow."
"1569","1557 - And al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, and we do not know of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrating from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1570","1558 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad and Alqamah, they said: While Abdullah was in his house, he said: Have these prayed? We said: No. He said: Stand and pray. And he did not command us with adhan nor iqamah. He said: So we went to stand behind him, so he took our hands and made us stand, placing one of us to his right and the other to his left. He said: Then when he bowed we placed our hands upon our knees. He said: So he struck our hands and clasped between his palms, then inserted them between his thighs. Then when he prayed he said: There will be rulers over you who delay prayer from its time to the east of the dead. So when you see them do that, pray the prayer at its time, then make your prayer with them supererogatory. And when you are three, pray together; and when you are more than that, let the eldest of you lead you. And when one of you bows, let him spread his forearms and thighs, then clasp between his palms. So it is as if I look at the interlacing of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, Mansur narrated it from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah similar to this; and the hadith of al-A'mash is more complete than the hadith of Mansur."
"1571","Remainder of the Musnad of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, and the beginning of the sixteenth, and it is the second of the hadith of Ibn Mas'ud. Mughirah from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1559 - Khallad ibn Aslam al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: an-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam and al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr five rak'ahs. So it was said to him: Has something been added to the prayer? So he said: And what is that? They said: You prayed five. He said: So he folded his leg and prostrated two prostrations."
"1572","1560 - And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. This hadith from al-Mughirah, we do not know anyone narrated it except Shu'bah, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Shu'bah except an-Nadr and Muhammad ibn Bakr. As for the hadith of al-Hakam, more than one narrated it from Shu'bah, and others than Shu'bah also narrated it."
"1573","1561 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, he said: That was mentioned by Shibak to Ibrahim, so he said: We asked Alqamah about that, so he narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba. So I said: And its writer and its two witnesses? So he said: We only narrate what we heard. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Mughirah with this chain except Jarir."
"1574","1562 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave, and {By those sent forth} was revealed to him, and a snake came out, so we rushed toward it, but it entered a hole. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You were protected from its evil as it was protected from your evil. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Mughirah except Abu Awanah."
"1575","1563 - Umar ibn Yahya al-Ayli narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The camel and the cow are for seven. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Mughirah except Hafs ibn Jumay'."
"1576","1564 - Ahmad ibn Malik al-Qushayri narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash, al-Mughirah, and Ibrahim ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me to recite while he was upon the minbar Surah an-Nisa'. So I recited until I reached: {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you over these as a witness}. Then his eyes filled with tears, and he said: Whoever is pleased to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad, and we heard it only from Ahmad ibn Malik; for he combined all these three in this hadith."
"1577","Husayn ibn Abdir-Rahman from Ibrahim from Alqamah. 1565 - Shu'ayb ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn, meaning Ibn Abdir-Rahman, from ash-Sha'bi and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that they said: When you doubt in the prescribed prayer, repeat; and when you doubt in the voluntary, prostrate two prostrations. He said: So I mentioned that to Ibrahim, so he said: What have you to do with this? Alqamah narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah said, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When one of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek the correct and prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness while sitting. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from ath-Thawri except Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham; and Husayn did not relate musnad from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1578","Isa ibn Qirtas from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1566 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Qirtas narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that a man came to him and said: I recited the Mufassal in one rak'ah. He said: Like the hasty recitation of poetry? I know the counterparts which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite or recite with: two surahs of the Mufassal in one rak'ah. And we do not know of Isa ibn Qirtas narrating from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1579","Yazid ibn al-Walid from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1567 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Walid, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that a man came to him and said to him: Do you know the counterparts well? So he said: Tonight I recited the Mufassal in one rak'ah. So he said: Like the hasty recitation of poetry, or scattering like the scattering of unripe dates? I knew the Qur'an which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite: twenty surahs from the beginning of the Mufassal, two surahs in one rak'ah. And we do not know of Yazid ibn al-Walid narrating from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1580","Abu Hamzah, whose name is Maymun, from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1568 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was brought al-Buraq and I rode it. When it came upon a mountain its legs would rise, and when it descended its hands would rise. So it carried us in a gloomy, foul land, then we emerged to a spacious, pleasant land. So he said - I think it is Jibril (peace be upon him): That is the land of the people of the Fire, and this is the land of the people of Paradise. Then I came upon a standing man, so he said: Who is this with you, O Jibril? He said: Your brother Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he welcomed and supplicated for me for blessing. So I said: Who is this, O Jibril? So he said: Your brother Isa son of Maryam (peace be upon him). Then we traveled and I heard a voice, then we came upon a man, so he said: Who is this with you? He said: This is your brother Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he welcomed and supplicated for me for blessing, and said: Ask for ease for your nation. So I said: Who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is your brother Musa. I said: Against whom was his complaint? He said: Against his Lord. I said: Against his Lord? He said: Yes; he knew his severity. Then we traveled and I saw something. So I said: What is this, or what is this, O Jibril? He said: This is the tree of your father Ibrahim; draw near to it. So we drew near to it, and he welcomed and supplicated for me for blessing. Then we proceeded until I came to Bayt al-Maqdis, so I tied the mount to the ring by which the prophets tie. Then we entered the mosque, and the prophets were presented to me, those Allah named of them and those He did not name. So I prayed with them except these three: Ibrahim, Musa, and Isa. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrates it from the hadith of Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except from this angle with this chain, and Hammad ibn Salamah alone narrates it from Abu Hamzah with this chain, from Abdullah."
"1581","1569 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform qunut except for one month; he did not perform qunut before it nor after it. And this hadith has been narrated from the hadith of Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah; Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated it from him. And we do not know anyone narrated this speech from Abu Hamzah except Sharik."
"1582","1570 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed his sandals, so those behind him removed theirs. So he said: What carried you to remove your sandals? They said: We saw you remove, so we removed. He said: Jibril informed me that in them was filth, so I removed them for that; do not remove your sandals. Ibrahim said: They would not remove them. He said: And I saw Ibrahim praying in his sandals. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except from the hadith of Abu Hamzah from him."
"1583","1571 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us a surah of the Qur'an, saying: Learn them, for there is no prayer except with tashahhud, saying: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except from this angle with this chain."
"1584","1572 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: Give every surah its due of bowing, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not combine of the Qur'an except twenty surahs of the Mufassal, meaning: he used to combine between two surahs in one rak'ah and more. And this hadith, we do not preserve it from the hadith of Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except from this angle."
"1585","1573 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn ar-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I was with Abdullah, then al-Ash'ath ibn Qays entered while he was eating lunch. So he said: Lunch, O Abu Abdir-Rahman; do you not know that today is the day of Ashura? He said: Yes; by the One in whose hand is my soul, I knew, and we were commanded to fast it before Ramadan was revealed. Then when Ramadan was revealed we were neither commanded nor forbidden regarding it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah except from the hadith of Abu al-Ahwas from him."
"1586","1574 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I used to see the whiteness of the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, twice. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Abu Hamzah with this chain except Mahbub ibn al-Hasan."
"1587","1575 - Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: He forbade wailing and said: It is of the affair of Jahiliyyah. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from the hadith of Abu Hamzah."
"1588","1576 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Among the nearness of the Hour is greeting by acquaintance, and he mentioned other speech."
"1589","1577 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that he disliked prayer in the mihrab and said: They were but churches, so do not resemble the People of the Book, meaning: he disliked prayer in the arch. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from the hadith of Abu Hamzah with this chain; and it enters the Musnad since he said: they were churches."
"1590","1578 - Ibrahim ibn Yusuf as-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah al-Kufi Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the khuffs: for the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night."
"1591","1579 - Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to me, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended to command Bilal to establish the prayer, then turn to people who heard the call and did not answer, and burn their houses over them. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim with this chain except from this angle, and we heard it only from Muqaddam."
"1592","Abu Hashim ar-Rummani, whose name is Yahya ibn Dinar, from Ibrahim from Alqamah. 1580 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Khuzi narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him a kunyah before a child was born to him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah except with this chain."
"1593","Ibn Awn from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1581 - Abdullah ibn as-Sabbah al-Attar and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, they said: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, that Abdullah used to teach a man the tashahhud, saying: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. So Abdullah repeated it upon him several times, each time saying: And I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, while the man said: And that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. So Abdullah said: Thus we were taught. And this hadith, I only entered it in the Musnad because he said: thus we were taught."
"1594","Farqad from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1582 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim as-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Abdus-Samad ibn Abdil-Warith narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Farqad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every kindness to a rich or poor person is charity. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdullah except from this angle with this chain."
"1595","Fudayl ibn Amr from Ibrahim from Alqamah from Abdullah. 1583 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, and he is Muhammad ibn Abdir-Rahman, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us istikhara: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, and I seek ability from You by Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty and mercy, for they are in Your hand; none owns them but You. For You know and I do not know, and You are able and I am not able, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this thing which is intended is good for me, then grant it and ease it; and if it is other than that, then decree for me good wherever it is. For You know and I do not know, and You are able and I am not able, and You are the Knower of the unseen. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Alqamah from Abdullah except from this angle musnad."
"1596","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Fudayl ibn 'Amr, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No one will enter Paradise who has the weight of a mustard seed of arrogance in his heart, and no one will enter the Fire who has the weight of a mustard seed of faith in his heart. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Aban ibn Taghlib, nor from Aban except Shu'bah."
"1597","Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj informed us, from Fudayl ibn 'Amr, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until he snored, then he stood up and prayed. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn 'Amr except al-Hajjaj, and a group narrated it from al-Hajjaj."
"1598","al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Salt ibn Bahram, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, that he used to scrape the two Mu'awwidhat (al-Falaq and al-Nas) from the mushaf and say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only commanded seeking refuge with them, and 'Abdullah would not recite them. And none of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) agreed with 'Abdullah on this statement, and it is established from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he recited them in prayer and that they were affirmed in the mushaf."
"1599","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, and from Muslim, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa'."
"1600","And Bishr narrated it to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Muslim, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And we do not know anyone who narrated this statement from Muslim, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, except Isra'il."
"1601","Ishaq ibn Buhlul narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Abu Shihab 'Abd Rabbihi ibn Nafi' narrated to me, from Muslim, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Hospitality is for three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity, and every good deed is charity. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from Muslim, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, except through the hadith of 'Abd Rabbihi, and we only heard it from Ishaq."
"1602","And 'Abd al-A'la ibn Wasil narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a house in which there were twelve men, and he said: In this house there is one whose trial for my ummah is more severe than the trial of the Dajjal. Abu Bakr al-Bazzar said: 'Ali ibn Thabit was a man of Kufa who was extreme in Shi'ism, and likewise Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, though the people of knowledge narrated from him and accepted his hadith, and Muslim was likewise, and none narrated this hadith other than them, and I think there was something else in the hadith besides these words."
"1603","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Tha'labah narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Himmani 'Abd al-Hamid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi and Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that he said: The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim died, and people said: The sun only eclipsed because of the death of Ibrahim, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life, so when you see that, pray. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi and Ibrahim except Habib ibn Hassan, and we do not know anyone who combined them except Abu Yahya al-Himmani."
"1604","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hani' Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasir narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah who said: We used to wipe with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over the leather socks: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"1605","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hani' narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasir narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the revelation (Surat al-Sajdah), and: Has there come upon man (Surat al-Insan)."
"1606","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah who said: I said to 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: Who was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn? He said: None of us was with him, except that we missed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that night, so we searched for him in the ravines and valleys, and we said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been snatched away, so we spent the worst night a people ever spent. When morning came, he appeared to us from the direction of Hira', so we said: O Messenger of Allah, we spent a night the like of which we never spent. He said: A caller of the jinn came to me — I think he said — they came, so I went to recite the Qur'an to them, and he took us and showed us their fires, and they asked him for provision, so he said: Every bone over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned falls into your hands."
"1607","Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, that one day he narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he said: this, or something like it."
"1608","al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Za'idah, from his father, from al-Sha'bi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman who buries her daughter alive and the buried girl are in the Fire. Ibn Abi Za'idah said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same. And we do not know anyone who authenticated it except Ibn Abi Za'idah, from his father."
"1609","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, that he said: The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim died, and people said: It only eclipsed because of the death of Ibrahim, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life, so when you see that, pray. Abu Ahmad said: Sufyan had narrated it to me, from Habib ibn Hassan, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Habib narrated it to us."
"1610","And 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hafs narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not clean yourselves with bones, for they are the provision of your brothers among the jinn. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one at length, but Hafs abridged this portion of it."
"1611","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah who said: Whoever wishes, I will swear to him that the short surah came down after the long surah: And for pregnant women, their term is until they deliver their burden. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one, but they did not say in it: from 'Alqamah."
"1612","'Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Harithi Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn Abi 'Isa informed me, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he cursed the eater of usury and its giver, its two witnesses and its writer, the woman who joins hair and the one who has it joined, the tattooer and the tattooed, the eyebrow-plucker and the one who has it done, and he forbade wailing."
"1613","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn Abi 'Isa narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed wine, its drinker and its pourer, its presser and the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier and the one to whom it is carried, its seller and its buyer, and the eater of its price. And we do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, except 'Isa ibn Abi 'Isa."
"1614","'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, about: You shall surely ride from stage to stage — O Muhammad — meaning: state after state. And Jabir narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, and from Jabir, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"1615","'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah who said: There is no fixed time nor number in prayer over the funeral, meaning the takbir."
"1616","'Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Badr Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in leather socks and sandals."
"1617","Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Alqamah and Abi al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The woman who buries her daughter alive and the buried girl are in the Fire. Thus Sharik narrated it."
"1618","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to relieve himself, and he said: Bring me three stones. So he brought him two stones and a piece of dung, so he took the two stones and threw away the dung. Thus Ma'mar said it, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah in this hadith."
"1619","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: 'Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhunan, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lending twice equals charity once. And we do not know that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhunan narrated from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, except this hadith, and we do not know anyone who raised it to the Prophet except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1620","'Abdullah ibn Sa'id and Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Duba'i narrated to us, they said: 'Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Kulayb, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, that he said: Shall I not show you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he said the takbir and raised his hands when he opened the prayer, then when he bowed he clasped his hands together and placed them between his thighs. When he finished praying he said: This is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did. And this hadith was narrated by 'Asim ibn Kulayb, and 'Asim has confusion in his hadith, especially in the hadith of raising the hands; he mentioned from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, that he raised his hands in the first takbir. And he narrated from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, that he raised his hands when he opened the prayer and when he raised his head from bowing, and he narrated from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that also, and he narrated from his father, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw him raising only the first time."
"1621","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh and Abu Dawud narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, and 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say the takbir at every lowering and rising, and would give salam to his right and to his left."
"1622","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, and 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"1623","'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to relieve himself. He said: Bring me three stones. So I searched and found two stones and a piece of dung. So he kept the two stones and threw away the dung, and said: It is filth."
"1624","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from 'Alqamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he used to give the people their stipends, then a man came and he gave him a thousand dirhams, then he said: Take it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Those before you were destroyed only by the dinar and the dirham, and they will destroy you."
"1625","And Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel."
"1626","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, he said: Shibak mentioned it, from Ibrahim, from Hunayy ibn Nuwayrah, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."
"1627","'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah informed us, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Hunayy ibn Nuwayrah, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. He said: And Abu 'Awanah did not mention Shibak."
"1628","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah who said: We used to say that the best of the people of Madinah was Ibn Abi Talib."
"1629","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn 'Ubaydullah al-Nakha'i, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd who said: 'Alqamah led us in Zuhr prayer with five rak'ahs. When he gave the salam, the people said: You prayed five, O Abu Shibl. He said: No, I did not do that. They said: Yes, you did. I was at the side of the people and I was a boy, so I said: Yes, you prayed five. He said to me: And you too, O one-eyed one, you say that? I said: Yes. So he turned around and prostrated twice, then gave the salam, then he said: 'Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in five rak'ahs. When he turned around, the people whispered among themselves, so he said: What is the matter with you? They said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been increased? He said: No. They said: You prayed five. So he turned around and prostrated twice, then gave the salam, then he said: I am only a human being; I forget as you forget."
"1630","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Qabisah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Hasan ibn 'Ubaydullah, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"1631","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave, and: By those sent forth in succession had been revealed to him. We were taking it fresh from his mouth when a snake came out against us. He said: Kill it. So we rushed to kill it but it escaped us. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah protected it from your harm as He protected you from its harm. And this hadith was narrated by Isra'il, who said: from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah and al-Aswad."
"1632","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded killing a snake in the Haram. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with this wording except Hafs."
"1633","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad and 'Alqamah, they said: We came to 'Abdullah at his house and he said: Have these people prayed? We said: No. He said: Then stand and pray. He did not command us with adhan or iqamah. He said: So we went to stand behind him, but he took our hands and placed us, putting one of us on his right and the other on his left. He said: When he bowed, we placed our hands on our knees, so he struck our hands and clasped his palms together, then inserted them between his thighs. When he finished praying he said: There will be rulers over you who delay the prayer from its time until near death, so when you see them do that, pray the prayer at its time, then make your prayer with them as supererogatory. When you are three, pray together, and when you are more than that, let one of you lead. When one of you bows, let him spread his forearms on his thighs, then clasp his palms together. It is as if I am looking at the interlacing of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with this wording except Ibrahim, from al-Aswad and 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah, though something similar has been narrated through other channels with different wordings."
"1634","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah who said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr with seven remaining, and seek it with nine, and seek it with eleven remaining, on the morning of Badr, for the sun rises every day between the two horns of Satan, except on the morning of Badr, when it rises white without rays. And this hadith was included by some people and inclined toward the musnad when he mentioned the morning of Badr."
"1635","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah and al-Aswad, that they entered upon 'Abdullah and he said: Have these people prayed? We said: No. So he stood between us, then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah, from al-A'mash."
"1636","'Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from Shibak, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah and al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, in a raised report, that he said: Which charity is best? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: That a man lend to his brother dirhams or the back of a riding animal."
"1637","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Shibak, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah or al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah."
"1638","And Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated it to us, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay' informed us, from Shibak, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah and al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I met a woman on one of the roads of Madinah and I took from her what is short of intercourse. He said: Then it was revealed: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds, the verse. They said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for him specifically or for people generally? He said: Rather, for people generally."
"1639","Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yazid ibn 'Ata', from Shibak, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah and al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina when the moon split."
"1640","Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisi narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to teach them the tashahhud in prayer: Salutations belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, except Za'idah, nor from Za'idah except Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Ju'fi."
"1641","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, who said: 'Abdullah used to teach us the tashahhud in prayer, drilling us on the alif and the waw."
"1642","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim and 'Umarah, from al-Aswad who said: 'Abdullah used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah of the Qur'an. And the hadith of Za'idah combined chains in it, making some like others: he mentioned from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah, from al-Aswad, and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah, and from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, with something similar to the hadith of Abu Wa'il. And we do not know anyone who combined these chains except Za'idah."
"1643","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la al-'Attar and Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, they said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, from Abu Hariz, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Lending twice equals charity once. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, except through this channel."
"1644","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn 'Asim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever consoles an afflicted person will have a reward like his. And this hadith was narrated by more than one as stopped (mawquf), but 'Ali ibn 'Asim and 'Abd al-Hakim raised it."
"1645","And Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he went deep into the valley when he stoned Jamrat al-'Aqabah, putting the mountain behind his back, then he stoned, and said: This is the station of the one to whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed. And this hadith was narrated by more than one, from Ibrahim, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, and thus Surayj narrated it, from Hammad, in what Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us."
"1646","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hisham, meaning Ibn Abi 'Abdullah, narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left in prayer. And we do not know anyone who raised it except Muslim, from Hisham. Others besides Muslim narrated it from Hisham, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from 'Abdullah, and Muslim sometimes did not mention al-Aswad and sometimes mentioned al-Aswad."
"1647","Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: 'Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: 'Utbah ibn Yaqzan narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from his maternal uncles, from 'Abdullah who said: The Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, if you are a prophet as you claim, tell us whence resemblance comes: a man resembles his paternal uncles at one time and his maternal uncles at another? Then he mentioned the hadith at length, and we have already brought it out in the hadith of 'Alqamah."
"1648","Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: 'Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: 'Utbah ibn Yaqzan narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from his maternal uncles, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the sperm falls into the womb, then he mentioned the hadith, and we have already mentioned it in the hadith of 'Alqamah, so we sufficed without repeating it after it."
"1649","Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Hakkam narrated to us, from 'Anbasah, from Jabir, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Witr is obligatory upon every Muslim. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel with this chain."
"1650","Muhammad ibn 'Umar al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah al-Nasri Abu Salamah, from Nahshal al-Qurashi, from al-Dahhak, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah who said: If the people of knowledge had guarded knowledge and placed it with its people, they would have led, but they narrated to worldly people to obtain some of their worldliness, so they became lowly to its people. I heard the Messenger of Allah say: Whoever makes worries into one worry, the worry of the Hereafter, Allah will suffice him the worry of this world, and whoever is pulled apart by worldly worries, Allah the Blessed and Exalted will not care in which of its valleys he perishes."
"1651","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah who said: Let none of you impose upon himself as a duty to leave to his right; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaving to his left most often. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated with this wording except from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, and we do not know a path for it except from al-Aswad, except a hadith in which Ziyad ibn 'Abdullah erred, narrating it from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah."
"1652","Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would most often leave to his left."
"1653","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this place two rak'ahs, then the prayer was established and he prayed four behind 'Uthman. I said: Did you forget? He said: No, but disagreement is evil."
"1654","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Jabir, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah, that he and 'Alqamah entered upon 'Abdullah, and he led us in prayer, standing between them, placing one on his right and the other on his left. Then we bowed and placed our hands on our knees, so he struck our hands, then clasped them, then placed them between his thighs. When he finished praying he said: This is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did."
"1655","'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah who said: It is of the Sunnah to conceal the tashahhud. And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel with this chain."
"1656","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed five, and when he gave the salam it was said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed five. So he prostrated twice, then gave the salam, then he said: I am only a human being; I forget as you forget."
"1657","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his need, and he said: Bring me three stones, and do not bring me a bone or dung."
"1658","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud and Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to relieve himself and said: Bring me three stones. So I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and threw away the dung, and said: It is filth. And this hadith was narrated by others besides Zuhayr, from Abu Ishaq, and there was disagreement over Abu Ishaq in its chain: Zuhayr said: from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah; al-Thawri said: from Abu Ishaq, from Abu 'Ubaydah, from 'Abdullah; Ma'mar said: from Abu Ishaq, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah; and Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah said: from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid."
"1659","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left."
"1660","al-Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Sayf narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Seek it on the night of the seventeenth of Ramadan, or the night of the twenty-first, or the night of the twenty-third, then he fell silent. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq with this chain except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah."
"1661","Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: So is there any who will remember."
"1662","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed five, and when he gave the salam he turned, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed five. So he prostrated twice, then gave the salam, then he said: I am only a human being; I forget as you forget. And we do not know this to be narrated from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, except through the hadith of Muhammad ibn Aban."
"1663","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited al-Najm and prostrated."
"1664","Muhammad ibn Jabir ibn Bujayr narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, that they were with 'Abdullah when a man came and greeted him, and he returned the greeting. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the nearness of the Hour is greeting only those one knows. And we do not know that al-Sha'bi narrated from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah, except this hadith."
"1665","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from al-Aswad, from 'Abdullah who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was feverish, so I placed my hand on him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you are suffering a severe fever. He said: We, the company of prophets, have our reward doubled — I think he said — and I suffer fever as two men among you suffer."
"1666","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah, meaning Ibn 'Umayr, from al-Aswad, who said: 'Abdullah narrated to us two hadiths, one from himself and the other from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 'Abdullah said: The believer sees his sins as if he is at the foot of a mountain fearing it will fall on him, while the hypocrite sees his sins like a fly that landed on something, and he waved it away like this and it flew. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Blessed and Exalted is more joyful at the repentance of the believer than a man who set out in a barren, deadly land with his camel carrying his provisions, food and drink, then he lost it. He went out seeking it until, when death overtook him, he said: I will return to the place where I lost it and die. So he returned and his eyes overcame him, then he woke to find his camel at his head with his provisions, food and drink upon it."
"1667","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from 'Abdullah, and from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah, with something similar."
"1668","Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Evil is it for one of them to say: I forgot verse such-and-such; rather, he was made to forget. Memorize the Qur'an, for it escapes from the chests of men more swiftly than camels from their hobbles."
"1669","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1670","And al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated it to us, he said: Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar to the hadith of Shu'bah. And we do not know a better path for these words from 'Abdullah than this path."
"1671","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The servant keeps telling the truth and seeking truthfulness until he is written with Allah as a siddiq, and he keeps lying and seeking falsehood until he is written with Allah as a liar."
"1672","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And we do not know this to be narrated from 'Abdullah with a better chain than this chain."
"1673","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Abusing a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, and it has been narrated from others besides Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1674","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a false oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a man, or the wealth of his brother, will meet Allah while He is angry with him, and concerning that was revealed: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price. And in this hadith Shu'bah combined al-A'mash and Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah. The hadith is well known from the hadith of al-A'mash, narrated by more than one from al-A'mash."
"1675","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Three traits, whoever has them is a hypocrite, and whoever has one trait has in him a trait of hypocrisy: when he speaks he lies, when he is trusted he betrays, and when he promises he breaks. And we do not know anyone who raised it except Abu Dawud, from Shu'bah with this chain; others besides Abu Dawud narrate it as stopped."
"1676","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is nearer to one of you than the strap of his sandal, and the Fire is likewise. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, as stopped, but al-Thawri raised it, from Mansur and al-A'mash."
"1677","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, will we be taken to account for what we did in the Jahiliyyah? He said: Whoever does good in Islam will not be taken to account for what he did in the Jahiliyyah, and whoever does evil in Islam will be taken for the first and the last."
"1678","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one, from Mansur, and by more than one from al-A'mash."
"1679","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) favored some people in the distribution, giving al-Aqra' ibn Habis a hundred camels, giving 'Uyaynah ibn Badr the same, and giving some Arabs, favoring them in the distribution. A man said: By Allah, he did not give justly — or: this is a distribution in which justice was not done, or the Face of Allah was not intended. I said: By Allah, I will surely inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of it. So I came to him and told him what the man said. His face changed and he said: Musa was harmed with more than this and he was patient. And this hadith was narrated by al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, except Jarir."
"1680","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: A man who slept the night until morning was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: That is a man in whose ears Satan has urinated. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Abdullah except Abu Wa'il, and we do not know a better chain for it from Abu Wa'il than this chain."
"1681","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Two women should not lie together naked and then describe her to her husband as if he is looking at her. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, with a better chain than this chain."
"1682","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il. And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated it to us, he said: Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il who said: We were at the door of 'Abdullah waiting for him, and he was late for us, so Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah said: I will bring him out to you. He entered to him, then 'Abdullah came out to us and said: I know of your place; nothing prevents me from coming out to you except dislike of boring you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to time us with admonition, disliking weariness for us. And we do not know this to be narrated from 'Abdullah except through the hadith of Abu Wa'il from him, and al-A'mash narrated it from Abu Wa'il."
"1683","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, that he said: You saw us when we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would send us without binding us in a matter until he did it. One of you will remain in good as long as he fears Allah, and when something troubles his soul he asks a man about it who cures him of it — and soon he may not find him. By Allah, I liken what has passed of this world only to a puddle whose clear water was drunk and whose murky water remains. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Wa'il through other than this channel, but we do not know a better path for it from Abu Wa'il than this path."
"1684","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1685","And Bishr ibn Khalid narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, al-A'mash, Hammad, Abu Hashim and al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1686","And Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, al-A'mash, Husayn, Abu Hashim and Hammad, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud: Salutations belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Hashim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except Shu'bah and al-Thawri."
"1687","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: How do I know that I am good? He said: When your neighbors say: You are good, then you are good; and when your neighbors say: You are bad, then you are bad. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Mansur except Ma'mar, and we do not know it to be narrated from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel."
"1688","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are three, two should not converse privately excluding the third until you mix with others, lest it grieve him. And these words have been narrated from 'Abdullah through other than the hadith of Mansur."
"1689","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: He drew lines and said: These are paths; upon every path among them is a devil calling to it, and he recited: And that this is My path, straight, so follow it, the verse. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from Abu Wa'il."
"1690","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing judged among people is blood, meaning on the Day of Resurrection. And thus Shu'bah narrated this hadith."
"1691","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man is with those he loves. And this hadith has been narrated from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Musa."
"1692","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: For every traitor there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except Shu'bah."
"1693","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one thing, and I say another: Whoever dies making a rival to Allah will enter the Fire, and I say: Whoever dies not making a rival to Allah will enter Paradise. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from Abu Wa'il, and by more than one from al-A'mash."
"1694","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il who said: A man said to 'Abdullah: Hayta laka, and 'Abdullah said: Thus we were taught. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1695","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"1696","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And we do not know a path for this hadith from 'Abdullah except this path."
"1697","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd; some people will be contested with me over it and I will be overcome regarding them, so I will say: O my Lord, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1698","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recounting a prophet whom his people struck while he wipes the blood from his face and says: Forgive my people, for they do not know. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1699","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which sin is greatest? He said: That you make a rival to Allah while He created you. He said: Then which? He said: That you kill your child fearing he will eat your food. He said: Then which? He said: That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife. Then he recited: And those who do not call upon another god with Allah nor kill the soul, the verse. And others besides Abu Mu'awiyah narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Amr ibn Shurahbil."
"1700","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No one is more jealous than Allah, and therefore He forbade indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is hidden; and no one loves praise more than Allah. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1701","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: We were walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed by Ibn Sa'id. He said: I have hidden something for you. He said: Dukh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be off; you will not exceed your limit. 'Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, let me strike his neck. He said: If he is the one you fear, you will not be able to kill him."
"1702","And Yahya ibn Habib ibn 'Arabi narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And we do not know this to be narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel."
"1703","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il who said: I was sitting with 'Abdullah and Abu Musa, and they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour there are days in which ignorance descends, knowledge is lifted, and harj increases. We said: What is harj? He said: Killing. And we do not know this to be narrated with this wording except with this chain."
"1704","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: We used to say in prayer: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon so-and-so, peace be upon so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Himself is Peace, so say: Salutations belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. When you say: Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, it reaches every righteous servant of Allah between heaven and earth. Then let one of you choose whatever supplication he likes. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1705","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you are three, two should not converse privately excluding the third."
"1706","Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew a line for us one day and said: This is the path of Allah. Then he drew lines and said: These are paths; upon every path among them is a devil calling to it, and he recited: And that this is My path, straight, the verse."
"1707","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il who said: We were at the door of 'Abdullah and he was late for us, so Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah said: I will bring him out to you. He entered to him, then 'Abdullah came out to us and said: I hear of your place, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except dislike of boring you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to time us with admonition, disliking weariness for us."
"1708","Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: None of you should say: I forgot verse such-and-such; rather, he was made to forget."
"1709","Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Answer the caller, do not refuse a gift, and do not strike the Muslims. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except 'Umar ibn 'Ubayd and Isra'il."
"1710","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"1711","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The sanctity of the wealth of the believer is like the sanctity of his blood. Abu Bakr said: And we do not know this hadith to be narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel with this chain, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash except Abu Shihab."
"1712","al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends good for a servant, He gives him understanding in religion and inspires him with his right course. And we do not know this to be narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash except Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub."
"1713","Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to his wife, let him cover himself and not strip naked like two donkeys. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except Mindal, and he erred in it. Sharik mentioned that he and Mindal were with al-A'mash, and with him was 'Asim al-Ahwal, and 'Asim narrated from Abu Qilabah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you goes to his wife, and he mentioned the hadith as disconnected."
"1714","Muhammad ibn 'Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il who said: 'Abdullah said: Allah the Blessed and Exalted looked into the hearts of servants and found the heart of Muhammad the best of the hearts of servants. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except 'Abd al-Salam."
"1715","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) favored some people in the distribution, giving al-Aqra' ibn Habis a hundred camels, giving 'Uyaynah ibn Badr the same, and giving some Arabs, favoring them in the distribution. A man said: By Allah, this is a distribution in which justice was not done, or the Face of Allah was not intended. I said: By Allah, I will surely inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of it. So I came to him and told him what the man said. His face changed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Musa was harmed with more than this and he was patient."
"1716","al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These five true prayers are expiations for the sins between them, as long as major sins are avoided. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash as raised except Salih ibn Musa, and he is weak in hadith. Others besides Salih narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, as stopped."
"1717","'Abbad ibn Ahmad al-'Arzami narrated to us, he said: my uncle Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydullah narrated to me, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr. And we do not know this to be narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel with this chain, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash except 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad, and we only heard it from 'Abbad ibn Ahmad."
"1718","'Abbad ibn Ahmad al-'Arzami narrated to us, he said: my uncle Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: By Allah, it is as if I hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk at the grave of 'Abdullah Dhu al-Bijadayn, with Abu Bakr and 'Umar, may Allah's mercy be upon them, saying: Lower your companion to me, until he laid him in his lahd. When he finished burying him, he faced the qiblah and said: O Allah, I have reached evening pleased with him, so be pleased with him. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad and Sa'd ibn al-Salt."
"1719","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, in a raised report, who said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except Sulayman ibn Qarm, and there is no harm in him."
"1720","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Abu Usamah and Abu Shihab narrated this hadith."
"1721","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd; some people will be contested with me over it and I will be overcome regarding them, so I will say: O my Lord, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"1722","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"1723","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding the tashahhud: Salutations belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"1724","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il who said: 'Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed. And Jarir narrated this hadith thus, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, while others besides Jarir narrated it from al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah ibn Hudhafah."
"1725","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one thing, and I say another. He said: Whoever dies making a rival to Allah will enter the Fire, and I say: Whoever dies not making a rival to Allah will enter Paradise. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except Abu 'Awanah."
"1726","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No one is more jealous than Allah, and therefore He forbade indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is hidden; and no one loves praise more than Allah. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Amr ibn Murrah except Shu'bah."
"1727","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, that a man came to him and said: I recited the Mufassal in one rak'ah. He said: Rattling like the rattling of poetry. I know the pairs that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite: two surahs of the Mufassal in one rak'ah. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except Shu'bah."
"1728","Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: A man of the people of al-Suffah died, and two dinars were found in his cloak, so that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Two brands. And Hammad ibn Zayd narrated this hadith from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, while Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah."
"1729","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Let not a woman lie with a woman and then describe her to her husband as if he is looking at her."
"1730","Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew a line for us one day and said: This is in the path of Allah. Then he drew lines and said: These are paths; upon every path among them is a devil calling to it, and he recited: And that this is My path, straight, so follow it, and do not follow the paths lest they separate you from His path. Then 'Asim described that to us, drawing to his right and to his left."
"1731","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: We used to count al-ma'un in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the bucket, the axe and the pot. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with this wording from 'Asim except Abu 'Awanah."
"1732","al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the revelation, and: Has there come upon man. And 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan narrated this hadith from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il and Zirr, from 'Abdullah."
"1733","'Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"1734","And 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid, meaning Sulayman ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Qays narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow up between Hajj and 'Umrah, for they remove poverty and sins as the bellows removes the dross of iron, gold and silver, and it has no reward less than Paradise. And we do not know this to be narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel."
"1735","Aws ibn Mukram al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Musa narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of you? They said: Yes. He said: The best of you are the best in character — I think he said — those of gentle sides. And we do not know this to be narrated from 'Abdullah except with this chain."
"1736","Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Za'idah, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour overtakes while they are alive, and those who take graves as mosques."
"1737","Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, meaning Ibn Qudamah, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the tashahhud: Salutations belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"1738","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another, and the Tulaqa' of Quraysh and the freedmen of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter. And I think Isra'il erred in this hadith when he narrated it from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, because the companions of 'Asim narrate it from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Jarir."
"1739","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Harami ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support: your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, the nearest then the nearest. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except this Ziyad."
"1740","'Abd al-Warith ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Aban ibn Yazid, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely punished people on the Day of Resurrection are a man who killed a prophet or was killed by a prophet, and an imam of misguidance. And we do not know anyone who raised it from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, except Aban."
"1741","1728 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim whose three children who have not reached puberty die except that Allah admits him to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them. It was said: And two? He said: And two. And this hadith was narrated by Za'idah, and it was narrated by 'Abd al-Samad, from Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1742","1729 - Al-'Abbas ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Ash'ath ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il and Zirr, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One."
"1743","1730 - Al-'Abbas narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il and Zirr, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salutation to his right and to his left. And we do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il and Zirr, except 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid."
"1744","1731 - Mu'adh ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man may utter a word by which he falls into the Fire for such-and-such autumns. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel with this chain."
"1745","1732 - And Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Ali ibn Manjuf narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: Ibn al-Nawwahah came as a messenger from Musaylimah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: I bear witness that Musaylimah is the messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I been one to kill a messenger, I would have killed you, or I would have struck your neck. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except al-Thawri."
"1746","1733 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il and Zirr, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One."
"1747","What 'Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah narrated from Abu Wa'il from 'Abdullah. 1734 - Raja' ibn Muhammad al-Saqati narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from 'Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should say: I forgot such-and-such verse; rather, he was made to forget."
"1748","1735 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-'Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Al-Mughirah ibn Mutarrif al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from 'Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, in a raised report, he said: The world is cursed; cursed is what is in it, except enjoining good, or forbidding evil, or remembrance of Allah. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from 'Abdullah ibn Thabit ibn Thawban with other than this chain, and we do not know anyone who followed Al-Mughirah ibn al-Mutarrif in this narration."
"1749","Al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah from Abu Wa'il. 1736 - Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Anbasah al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Badal ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the tashahhud, then he mentioned the hadith in full. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, except Badal ibn al-Muhabbar."
"1750","1737 - Mahmud ibn Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: 'Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: When we sat in prayer for the tashahhud we used to say: Peace be upon Allah before His servants, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mika'il; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us to say in the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"1751","1738 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn 'Adi, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Laylat al-Qadr, and he said: I had been informed of it, then it slipped away from me, so seek it in nine remaining, or three remaining. And we do not know that al-Zubayr ibn 'Adi narrated from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except this hadith."
"1752","And from what 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated from Abu Wa'il from 'Abdullah. 1739 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Hamid, narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1753","1740 - And Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah expressed disapproval to us of conversing after 'Isha. And we do not know that 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except this hadith."
"1754","And from what Fudayl ibn 'Amr narrated from Abu Wa'il. 1741 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad Abu Shaybah al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Fudayl ibn 'Amr, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who guides to good is like its doer. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel with this chain."
"1755","1742 - And Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Fudayl ibn 'Amr, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he taught them the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. And we do not know that Fudayl ibn 'Amr narrated from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, except these two hadiths."
"1756","And from what Jami' ibn Rashid narrated from Abu Wa'il from 'Abdullah. 1743 - Al-Husayn ibn Abi Zayd al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Abi Rashid and 'Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one who dies leaving wealth for which he does not pay zakat except that Allah will make for him on the Day of Resurrection a collar around his neck, a bald serpent, so he flees from it while it follows him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to us its confirmation in the Book of Allah: And let not those who withhold what Allah has given them of His bounty think it is good for them; rather it is evil for them. They will be collared with what they withheld on the Day of Resurrection. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Jami' ibn Abi Rashid, nor from 'Abd al-Malik, except Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah."
"1757","1744 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Abi Rashid, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he taught them the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. He said: And he teaches us this supplication as he teaches us the Qur'an: O Allah, set right what is between us, join our hearts, guide us to the paths of peace, keep us away from indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is hidden. O Allah, bless for us our hearing, our sight, our spouses, our offspring, and turn to us, indeed You are the Oft-Returning, the Merciful. O Allah, make us thankful for Your blessing, praising it and accepting it, and complete it upon us, O Most Merciful of the merciful. And this hadith with this wording, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Jami' ibn Abi Rashid, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1758","1745 - Al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Abi Rashid, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever swears an oath in order to cut off thereby the property of a Muslim man will meet Allah while He is angry with him. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Ibn 'Uyaynah, from Jami'."
"1759","Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Abu Wa'il from 'Abdullah. 1746 - Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: I know the paired surahs with which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray: The Winnowing Winds, The Mount, The Star, The Moon Has Drawn Near, The Occurrence, Nun and the Pen, The Reality, The Questioner Asked, The Enwrapped, The Cloaked, I Do Not Swear by the Day of Resurrection, Has There Come Upon Man, The Emissaries, About What Do They Question, The Pluckers, He Frowned, When the Sun Is Folded, Woe to the Defrauders, and Ha-Mim, the Smoke. And we do not know anyone who brought this hadith with this wording except Salamah ibn Kuhayl, and we do not know that Salamah narrated from Abu Wa'il except this hadith."
"1760","And from what Abu Nahshal narrated from Abu Wa'il from 'Abdullah. 1747 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abu Nahshal, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: 'Umar surpassed the people in three matters: concerning the captives on the day of Badr, for he wanted to kill them, so Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah, you would have been touched; the verse; and concerning the mention of the veil: he commanded the wives of the Prophet to veil themselves, so Zaynab said to him: What do you want, O son of al-Khattab, while revelation descends in our houses? So Allah, blessed and exalted, sent down: And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a veil; and the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Allah, strengthen Islam with 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. And we do not know these words as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel with this chain."
"1761","And from what Wasil narrated from Abu Wa'il from 'Abdullah. 1748 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Wasil, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah that he said: We have heard the recitation, and I remember those which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite: eighteen surahs from the Mufassal, and two surahs from Al Ha-Mim. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud."
"1762","And from what al-Mu'alla ibn 'Irfan narrated from Abu Wa'il from 'Abdullah. 1749 - Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, he said: Al-Mu'alla ibn 'Irfan narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il say: I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you - and this day of yours is a sacred day - like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. And we do not know these words as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel."
"1763","1750 - And Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, he said: Al-Mu'alla ibn 'Irfan narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: On the day of Badr I came upon Abu Jahl while life still remained in him, so I cut off his head, then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him."
"1764","1751 - Al-'Abbas ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Abdullah, a man from Kufa, narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Mu'alla ibn 'Irfan, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe three times into the vessel. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel with this chain."
"1765","And from what Sam'an al-Maliki narrated from Abu Wa'il from 'Abdullah. 1752 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Sam'an al-Maliki, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah who said: A Bedouin, a very old shaykh, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: No; by the One who sent you with the truth, I have not prepared for it much prayer nor fasting, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with whom you love. He said: Then the old man jumped up and urinated in the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, perhaps he is among the people of Paradise, and he poured water over his urine."
"1766","Al-'Ala' ibn Khalid from Abu Wa'il. 1753 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from his father, from al-'Ala' ibn Khalid, from Shaqiq, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the statement of Allah, blessed and exalted: And Hell is brought that Day. He said: It is brought, led with seventy thousand reins, with each rein seventy thousand angels."
"1767","1754 - And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated it to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-'Ala' ibn Khalid, from Shaqiq, from 'Abdullah, similarly, raising it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1768","1755 - And 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated it to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-'Ala' ibn Khalid, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah similarly, but he did not raise it. And we do not know anyone who raised this hadith except 'Umar ibn Hafs, from his father; and al-'Ala' is well known, al-Thawri narrated from him."
"1769","Husayn from Abu Wa'il. 1756 - Al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I am your forerunner at the Pond; some people will be contested with me over them and I will be overcome regarding them, so I will surely say: My companions; then it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"1770","And from what 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah narrated from 'Abdullah. 1757 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Humran narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from 'Abdullah ibn Ma'bad al-Zimmani, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from his uncle 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: This verse was revealed concerning a group of Arabs who used to worship a group of jinn; then the jinn became Muslim while the group of Arabs did not know, and that is His statement: Say: Call upon those whom you claim besides Him, for they have no power to remove harm from you nor to change it; the verse. And we only included this hadith in the Musnad of 'Abdullah because he said in it: It was revealed; and we do not know any hadith with this meaning narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1771","1758 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi 'Ata', from Mihsan ibn 'Ali, from 'Awn ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from his father, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The one who remembers Allah among the heedless is like the fighter among those who flee. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel with this chain."
"1772","1759 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from his father, from 'Abdullah, in a raised report, he said: Whoever's eyes shed tears like a fly's wing out of fear of Allah will not enter the Fire until milk returns to the udder. And we do not know these words as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel with this chain; and Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd is not strong, and he is a well-known man from Medina."
"1773","1760 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from his father, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he smiled, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, at what did you smile? He said: I marvel at the believer and his panic at sickness; had he known what is in store for him in sickness, he would love to remain sick until he meets Allah. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel."
"1774","1761 - Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Hudayj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, and he mentioned the story of the Negus."
"1775","1762 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Azraqi narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn 'Abdullah, from his father, from 'Abdullah, that a rooster crowed in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a man reviled it, so he forbade reviling the rooster. And in this hadith Muslim ibn Khalid erred; the correct version is from Salih ibn Kaysan, from 'Ubaydullah, from Zayd ibn Khalid."
"1776","Zayd ibn Wahb from 'Abdullah. 1763 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1777","1764 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1778","1765 - And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah and Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty days, then he is a clot for the same period, then he is a lump for the same period, then Allah sends the angel to him and he is commanded with four words; it is said: Write his term, his deeds, his provision, and whether wretched or blessed. For one of you may do the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is only a cubit between him and it, then the writing overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of the Fire and enters it; and a man may do the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is only a cubit between him and it, then he does the deeds of the people of Paradise - I think he said: and enters it. And this hadith was narrated by al-A'mash, from Zayd, from 'Abdullah, and more than one narrated it from al-A'mash with this chain; and Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated it, from Zayd, from 'Abdullah."
"1779","1766 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us with it, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Fitr, meaning Ibn Khalifah, narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of al-A'mash."
"1780","1767 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Hamid, narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me there will be favoritism and matters you will disapprove of. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command whoever among us reaches that? He said: You will render the duty upon you, and ask Allah for what is yours. And we do not know this hadith with this wording as narrated except from 'Abdullah, and we do not know any path for it from 'Abdullah except this path; and it was narrated from others besides 'Abdullah with other than this wording."
"1781","1768 - 'Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb who said: It was said to 'Abdullah: What about al-Walid ibn 'Uqbah, whose beard drips wine? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from spying, and if something becomes apparent to us we will change it. And we do not know anyone who raised it with a chain except Asbat; and others besides Asbat narrated it, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah, that he said: Allah forbade us from spying."
"1782","1769 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated to us, he said: Warqa', meaning Ibn 'Umar, narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1783","1770 - And Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated it to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Peace is a name among the names of Allah which He placed on earth, so spread it among you. For when a Muslim man passes by people and greets them and they return it to him, he has a degree of merit over them for reminding them of peace; and if they do not return it to him, one who is better and purer than them returns it to him. And this hadith was narrated by more than one as stopped; and Warqa', Sharik, and Ayyub ibn Jabir raised it with a chain."
"1784","1771 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Umar al-Rumi narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'id, the guide of al-A'mash, narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people of the chambers, the Fire has been kindled; had you known what I know, you would laugh little and weep much. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except 'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'id with this chain, and we do not know it as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel."
"1785","1772 - 'Abd al-Warith ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If two men enter Islam then abandon one another, one of them is outside Islam until he returns - meaning: the wrongdoer among them."
"1786","1773 - Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah who said: We did not perform ablution on account of treading. And Yazid narrated this hadith thus, from Sharik; and others besides Sharik narrated it, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il."
"1787","1774 - Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, that 'Abdullah was in Hims and recited Surah Yusuf, whereupon a man said: It was not revealed thus. He said: Then he smelled the odor of wine from him and said: You drink filth and deny revelation. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Zayd, from 'Abdullah, except Sharik."
"1788","1775 - Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn 'Amir al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After you there are days of patience; patience in them is like grasping hot coals; for the doer in them is the reward of fifty. They said: O Messenger of Allah, fifty of them or fifty of us? He said: Fifty of you. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel."
"1789","'Abidah al-Salmani from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. 1776 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. And we do not know any path for this hadith from 'Abdullah except this path."
"1790","1777 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur. And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah who said: A scholar, or a man from the People of the Book, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim, has it reached you that Allah, blessed and exalted, carries creation upon a finger, the trees upon a finger, and the earth upon a finger; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared. Yahya said: And Fudayl ibn 'Iyad added, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah who said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed in wonder and affirmation. And this hadith was narrated by Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah; and al-A'mash said: From Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah; and 'Amr ibn Talhah erred in it, narrating it from Asbat, from Mansur, from Khaythamah, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah."
"1791","1778 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Recite to me. I said: Did I not learn from you? He said: I love to hear it from other than me. He said: So I recited to him Surah al-Nisa until I reached: Then how when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you against these as a witness; he said: Then his eyes overflowed. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ibrahim, from 'Ubaydah, from 'Abdullah, except al-A'mash; and Abu al-Ahwas and al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad narrated it, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdullah."
"1792","1779 - 'Abdah ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah, in a raised report, he said: Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour overtakes while alive, and those who take graves as mosques. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash with this chain except Qays."
"1793","1780 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Azhar narrated to us, from Ibn 'Awn, from Ibrahim, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah, in a raised report, he said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn 'Awn, from Ibrahim, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah, except Azhar."
"1794","1781 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah al-Dashtaki narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from 'Abidah al-Salmani, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last of the people of Paradise to enter and the last of the people of the Fire to exit is a man who says: My Lord, take me out of this Fire to the shade of this tree; then when relief reaches him he looks at the trees of Paradise and says: My Lord, this one. He said: Then he comes out, having no deeds to carry him forth, so he comes out crawling until he reaches - meaning Paradise - and finds no dwelling in it, so he returns to the Lord, blessed and exalted, and says: My Lord, I found no dwelling in it for me. He says: Go, for you have the like of the world and ten times its like. He said: So that is the least of the people of Paradise in share. He said: Are You mocking me while You are my Lord? He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars and teeth appeared. And we do not know it as narrated from the hadith of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Ibrahim, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah, except from the hadith of 'Amr, from Abu Qays from him."
"1795","1782 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah."
"1796","1783 - And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated it to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Salih al-'Ijli narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah."
"1797","1784 - And Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated it to us, he said: Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to teach them: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with this chain except Qays."
"1798","Harithah ibn Mudarrib from 'Abdullah. 1785 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib who said: A man went out wanting to graze his horse, then passed by the mosque of Banu Hanifah and entered to pray, when his imam was reciting the words of Musaylimah the liar. So he came to 'Abdullah and informed him, and he sent to them and sought their repentance, and they repented, except 'Abdullah ibn al-Nawwahah, for he said to him: O 'Abdullah ibn al-Nawwahah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Were it not that you are a messenger I would strike your neck; but today you are no messenger. O so-and-so, stand to him and strike his neck. And we do not know anyone who narrated these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) higher than 'Abdullah, even if it is narrated from 'Abdullah through other than this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah, from 'Abdullah, raised, except Abu Mu'awiyah."
"1799","1786 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly, or close to it. And we do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, and raised it with a chain except Abu Mu'awiyah; and we do not know anyone who raised the hadith of al-Thawri with a chain except Muhammad ibn Kathir."
"1800","'Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Hadi from 'Abdullah. 1787 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn 'Athmah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Kaysan, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The closest of you to me on the Day of Resurrection are those who send most blessings upon me in the world. Thus Muhammad ibn Khalid narrated it."
